window.p1Answers=[{"b":"02","t":1,"i":0,"en":"Not really, to be honest. I'm good with faces, but names just slip away. At parties or dinners I hear a name only once, and by the time I want to introduce the person, it's gone. So no, it's not easy for me.","cn":"老实说不太容易。我记脸还行，但名字就是溜得快。聚会或吃饭时名字往往只听过一遍，等我想介绍对方时，已经忘了。所以说对我来说并不容易。"},{"b":"02","t":1,"i":1,"en":"I have a couple of tricks. I repeat the name out loud when I first hear it, and I try to link it to something familiar, like a friend or a film. If it's an unusual name, it sticks much more easily. It still takes me two or three meetings, though.","cn":"我有几个小办法。第一次听到时我会把名字念出来，还尽量把它和熟悉的东西联系起来，比如某个朋友或电影。如果名字比较特别，就更容易记住。不过还是得见两三次才记得住。"},{"b":"02","t":1,"i":2,"en":"Honestly, it feels a bit awkward. I know it's usually not personal — people are just busy or bad with names, like me — but there's still a small moment of 'oh, I wasn't memorable'. I try not to take it seriously, though, and I just say my name again with a smile.","cn":"说实话有点尴尬。我知道通常不是针对我——大家只是忙或者像我一样记性差——但还是会有那么一瞬间觉得'哦，我不够让人记住'。不过我尽量不当真，就笑着再说一遍我的名字。"},{"b":"02","t":1,"i":3,"en":"Yes, quite often, actually. It's probably my worst memory habit. I'll meet someone, chat for ten minutes, and then completely forget their name by the next day. That's exactly why I've started using little tricks to hold onto them.","cn":"其实挺经常的。这可能是我最差的记忆习惯。我会见到某人、聊上十分钟，第二天就完全忘了对方叫什么。也正是因为这个，我开始用一些小技巧来记住名字。"},{"b":"02","t":2,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I remember it clearly. I was nervous and excited at the same time — new uniform, new building, new faces everywhere. My mum walked me to the gate, and I remember feeling very small in that huge playground. It's a day that really stayed with me.","cn":"记得很清楚。我既紧张又兴奋——新校服、新教学楼、到处都是新面孔。我妈把我送到门口，我记得自己在那个大操场上觉得特别渺小。那一天真的留在我的记忆里。"},{"b":"02","t":2,"i":1,"en":"Yes, a few. Maths was the hardest for me — I just couldn't keep up with the teacher's speed. Science was tricky too, especially the experiments. But I have to say, struggling with them actually taught me how to study properly in the end.","cn":"有几门。数学对我最难——我跟不上老师的节奏。科学也难，尤其是实验。但我得说，正是这些困难最后教会了我怎么好好学习。"},{"b":"02","t":2,"i":2,"en":"My favourite subject was English. It didn't feel like work to me, because I loved reading stories and learning new words. My teacher was also very kind and made every lesson fun. That's probably why I'm still interested in languages today.","cn":"我最喜欢英语。它对我来说不像任务，因为我喜欢读故事、学新单词。我的老师也很亲切，让每节课都很有趣。这可能就是我现在还喜欢语言的原因。"},{"b":"02","t":2,"i":3,"en":"Yes, I miss the easy friendships, honestly. You saw your friends every single day, and everything felt simple. I also miss having so much free time. University is more independent, but it's also more stressful. Sometimes I really miss those carefree days.","cn":"其实我很怀念那份轻松的友谊。那时每天都能见到朋友，一切都简单。我也怀念有那么多自由时间。大学更独立，但也更有压力。有时我真的很怀念那些无忧无虑的日子。"},{"b":"02","t":3,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I like buying shoes, but I'm not crazy about it. I probably buy a new pair every three or four months, usually when the old ones are worn out. I go for trainers most of the time, because I walk a lot and they're comfortable.","cn":"我喜欢买鞋，但不算特别狂热。大概每三四个月买一双，通常是旧鞋穿坏了。大多数时候我买运动鞋，因为我走路多，穿着舒服。"},{"b":"02","t":3,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I have, a couple of times. It's convenient and often cheaper, but there's a risk — the size can be wrong or the material feels different from the photos. So now I only buy online from shops I already know, and I check the reviews carefully.","cn":"买过，有几次。网上买方便、也常常更便宜，但有风险——尺码可能不对，或者材质和照片看起来不一样。所以现在我只在熟悉的店里网购，还会仔细看评价。"},{"b":"02","t":3,"i":2,"en":"Honestly, not that much — maybe a few hundred yuan a pair. I'd rather spend money on good quality that lasts than on a cheap pair that falls apart in a month. But I never go for designer brands; that feels like a waste to me.","cn":"说实话不太多——一双可能几百块。我宁愿花在耐穿的好质量上，也不买一个月就散架的便宜货。但我从不买设计师大牌，那对我来说像是浪费。"},{"b":"02","t":3,"i":3,"en":"Comfortable shoes, definitely. I've learned my lesson — I once bought a beautiful pair that hurt my feet all day, and I never wore them again. If a shoe isn't comfortable, it doesn't matter how nice it looks. So I always choose comfort first.","cn":"绝对选舒服的鞋。我吃过亏——买过一双好看的鞋，穿一天脚都疼，后来再也没穿过。如果鞋不舒服，再好看也没用。所以我总是舒服优先。"},{"b":"02","t":4,"i":0,"en":"I eat fruit every day, usually an apple or a banana with breakfast. Vegetables I have at least twice a day, with lunch and dinner. I try to keep it balanced, though I have to admit I still love fried food.","cn":"我每天都吃水果，通常是早饭时一个苹果或香蕉。蔬菜一天至少吃两次，午饭和晚饭都会吃。我尽量保持均衡，不过得承认我还是爱吃油炸的。"},{"b":"02","t":4,"i":1,"en":"I usually buy them at a small market near my flat, because the vegetables there are fresher and cheaper than in supermarkets. Fruit I sometimes order online, especially in summer when it's too hot to go out. The market is my main place, though.","cn":"我一般在离家不远的小市场买，因为那儿的菜比超市更新鲜、也更便宜。水果有时我会网购，尤其夏天太热懒得出门的时候。不过市场还是我的主要选择。"},{"b":"02","t":4,"i":2,"en":"I'm not a big fan of bitter vegetables like bitter melon, honestly. And I don't like durian either, though I know a lot of people love it. It's really the smell — I just can't get past it.","cn":"说实话我不太喜欢苦瓜这类苦味的菜。榴莲我也不喜欢，虽然我知道很多人爱它。主要是那个味道，我就是接受不了。"},{"b":"02","t":4,"i":3,"en":"Yes, definitely. As a kid I hated onions and carrots — I used to pick them out of my food and hide them. I also refused to eat tomatoes unless they were in sauce. Funny enough, I eat all of them now.","cn":"当然有。小时候我特别讨厌洋葱和胡萝卜——我会把它们挑出来藏起来。番茄除非做成酱，否则我也不吃。有意思的是，现在这些我全都吃了。"},{"b":"02","t":4,"i":4,"en":"Yes, quite a lot, especially older people. In my city, many families grow a few vegetables on their balcony or in a small garden if they have one. My aunt grows tomatoes and chillies at home. I think it's both a hobby and a way to save a bit of money.","cn":"是的，挺多的，尤其是老人。在我市，很多家庭会在阳台或小院里种点菜。我姑姑就在家种番茄和辣椒。我觉得这既是个爱好，也能省点钱。"},{"b":"02","t":5,"i":0,"en":"Yes, all the time — they're everywhere online. Every time I open an app or scroll through social media, there's an advert popping up. I'd say I see dozens a day, most of which I just ignore without even thinking.","cn":"是的，一直都能看到——网上到处都是。每次我打开App或者刷社交媒体，都会弹出广告。我一天大概能看到几十个，其中大部分我根本不用想就忽略了。"},{"b":"02","t":5,"i":1,"en":"Yes, one really stuck with me. It was a soft drink advert at Chinese New Year, with a big family all sitting around a table. It was warm and cheerful, and it made me feel that holidays are about being together. Even now, that ad reminds me of my own family dinners.","cn":"有一个印象特别深。那是一支春节的饮料广告，一大家子人围着桌子坐在一起。它温暖又欢乐，让我觉得节日就是团聚。直到现在，那支广告还会让我想起自己家的团圆饭。"},{"b":"02","t":5,"i":2,"en":"Yes, quite a lot. There are posters on the walls and screens on the platforms that play adverts on a loop. The interesting thing is that people are so used to them that most of us don't even notice them any more. We just stare at our phones instead.","cn":"是的，挺多的。墙上有海报，站台的屏幕上循环播放广告。有意思的是，人们太习惯了，我们大多数人根本不注意它们，反而都低头看手机。"},{"b":"02","t":5,"i":3,"en":"Honestly, not really — most of them annoy me, especially the ones that pop up and won't close. But I don't hate all of them. If an advert is clever or funny, I can actually enjoy it. The problem is that most are just loud and repetitive.","cn":"说实话不太喜欢——大部分让我烦，尤其是那种弹出来还关不掉的。但也不是全都讨厌。如果一则广告有创意或者好笑，我其实会欣赏。问题是大多数广告又吵又重复。"},{"b":"02","t":5,"i":4,"en":"I like adverts that tell a little story rather than shouting about the product. My favourite ones are short and simple, with nice music and real people in them. If an advert makes me smile or think, that works for me. Cold hard selling just puts me off.","cn":"我喜欢那种讲一个小故事的广告，而不是一味吹产品的。我最喜欢短小简单、配好听的音乐、有真实人物出镜的。如果一则广告能让我笑或者让我想一想，那就有效。生硬地硬推销只会让我反感。"},{"b":"02","t":5,"i":5,"en":"Yes, I have a few times, though not often. Once I bought a snack I saw in a funny advert, and it turned out I actually liked it. But I'm usually quite careful — I know adverts are designed to make things look better than they are, so I don't trust them completely.","cn":"买过几次，不过不多。有一次我买了一个在搞笑广告里看到的零食，结果我还挺喜欢的。但我通常比较小心——我知道广告就是为了把东西拍得比实际好，所以我不完全相信它们。"},{"b":"02","t":6,"i":0,"en":"Yes, quite a few. My parents encouraged me to try different things — I did swimming, drawing and even a bit of piano. I didn't stick with all of them, but I'm glad I had the chance. Trying things out is how you find what you really like.","cn":"有挺多的。我父母鼓励我尝试不同的东西——我学过游泳、画画，还学过一点钢琴。我没能全都坚持下来，但我很高兴我有这些机会。多尝试，才能找到自己真正喜欢的东西。"},{"b":"02","t":6,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I think they should, within reason. Trying lots of things helps you discover your strengths and meet different people. Of course, you shouldn't just jump from one thing to the next without committing — but having a go at something new is usually worth it.","cn":"我觉得应该，只要合理就行。多尝试能帮你发现自己的长处，也能认识不同的人。当然，不该什么都不投入就一个接一个地换——但去试试新东西通常是值得的。"},{"b":"02","t":6,"i":2,"en":"Yes, I do, as long as I have the time. If something new comes up and it looks interesting, I'm usually happy to give it a try. I'd rather regret doing something than regret missing out on it. That's sort of my attitude.","cn":"喜欢，只要我有时间。如果有新机会出现、看起来又有意思，我通常乐意试试。我宁愿后悔做过某事，也不愿后悔错过它。这差不多是我的态度。"},{"b":"02","t":6,"i":3,"en":"Not as often as I'd like, honestly. New opportunities usually come from being in the right place or knowing the right people, and right now I'm mostly focused on my studies. But I try to say yes whenever something good comes along.","cn":"说实话，没有我希望的那么多。新机会通常来自在对的地方、认识对的人，而我现在主要专注学习。但只要有好事出现，我都会尽量说好。"},{"b":"02","t":7,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I always try to get a window seat if I can. I love watching the view go past — fields, rivers, small towns you'd never see otherwise. It makes a long trip feel much shorter, and it's calmer than staring at a screen.","cn":"是的，可以的话我总是尽量要个靠窗的座位。我喜欢看风景往后退——田野、河流、平时根本看不到的小镇。它让长途旅行感觉短多了，也比盯着屏幕平静。"},{"b":"02","t":7,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I did. When I was small, we took a long train ride to visit my grandparents, and it took almost a whole day. I remember being bored at first, but my mum brought snacks and played games with me. Looking back, it was quite special.","cn":"有的。小时候我们坐很久的火车去看爷爷奶奶，差不多要一整天。我记得一开始觉得无聊，但我妈带了零食、还陪我玩游戏。回想起来，那趟旅程挺特别的。"},{"b":"02","t":7,"i":2,"en":"Not as often as I should, to be honest. I have a bike, but I mostly use it for short trips — to the market or around the park. The city isn't very bike-friendly because of the traffic, so I'm a bit careful about riding on busy roads.","cn":"说实话，没有我应该骑的那么多。我有辆自行车，但主要用来办点小事——去市场或者在公园附近转。因为车多，这座城市对自行车不算友好，所以我在繁忙的路上骑得比较小心。"},{"b":"02","t":7,"i":3,"en":"For everyday travel I use the bus or the metro, because it's cheap and I can read on the way. For longer trips I prefer the train — it's comfortable and you get to see the countryside. I only fly when the distance is really long.","cn":"日常出行我坐公交或地铁，因为便宜、路上还能看书。长途我更喜欢火车——舒服，还能看郊外的风景。只有距离真的很远时我才会坐飞机。"},{"b":"02","t":8,"i":0,"en":"Yes, quite often, especially in the evening. By the time I finish studying and everything else, I'm usually worn out. I think it's normal for students, but I try to manage it with sleep and exercise rather than just pushing through.","cn":"是的，挺经常的，尤其是晚上。等我学完、忙完别的事，通常就累到不行了。我觉得这对学生来说很正常，但我尽量靠睡眠和运动来调节，而不是硬撑。"},{"b":"02","t":8,"i":1,"en":"Mostly in the late afternoon or evening. There's a slump after lunch, and again around nine at night when I've been focusing for a long time. If I don't sleep well the night before, I feel tired all day, not just at one point.","cn":"大多是在下午晚些时候或晚上。午饭后会犯困，晚上九点左右、专注很久之后也会。如果前一晚没睡好，我就会整天都累，而不只是某个时段。"},{"b":"02","t":8,"i":2,"en":"If I'm tired, I usually take a short break rather than fight it. I'll have a glass of water, stretch a bit, or step outside for some fresh air. If it's really bad, I take a twenty-minute nap, which works wonders. Coffee is my last choice.","cn":"累了的话，我通常会短暂休息，而不是硬扛。我会喝杯水、拉伸一下，或者出去透透气。如果实在很累，我就睡个二十分钟的小觉，效果特别好。咖啡是我的最后选择。"},{"b":"02","t":8,"i":3,"en":"Yes, usually I still go. Being with friends actually wakes me up, so I often feel better after I'm out. But if I'm really exhausted, I'll cancel and stay in — I've learned that pushing myself too hard just makes the next day worse.","cn":"一般还是会去。和朋友在一起其实能让我精神起来，所以出门后我常常感觉更好。但如果我真的累到不行，我就会取消、待在家里——我学到硬撑只会让第二天更糟。"},{"b":"02","t":9,"i":0,"en":"Mostly from my parents and teachers. My mum always reminded me to say thank you and hello, and at school we were taught to be respectful to teachers and older people. I think politeness is something you pick up by watching the people around you, more than by being told.","cn":"主要来自父母和老师。我妈总提醒我要说谢谢和你好，学校里也教我们要尊敬老师和长辈。我觉得礼貌更多是看着身边的人学会的，而不是被说教出来的。"},{"b":"02","t":9,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I think it's very important. Being polite makes everyday life smoother and shows respect for other people. It doesn't cost anything, but it can make someone's whole day better. Even a simple thank you can change the mood of a conversation.","cn":"我觉得非常重要。有礼貌让日常生活更顺畅，也表达了对别人的尊重。它不花一分钱，却能让别人一整天心情更好。甚至一句简单的谢谢，都能改变一场对话的气氛。"},{"b":"02","t":9,"i":2,"en":"I'd say almost everywhere, but especially when meeting someone new, visiting someone's home, or eating with others. Also when you need help — a polite request works far better than a rude demand. Basically, any time you're dealing with people, politeness matters.","cn":"我觉得几乎任何场合都需要，但尤其是初次见面、去别人家做客、或者和别人一起吃饭时。还有就是需要帮忙时——礼貌的请求比粗鲁的要求有效得多。基本上，只要是在和人打交道，礼貌就重要。"},{"b":"02","t":9,"i":3,"en":"As a child, I was taught to greet people with a proper hello, to say thank you for gifts, and to give up my seat to older people. Small things, really, but they became habits. I remember being shy, so my parents would gently remind me to speak up.","cn":"小时候，我被教着要好好地跟人打招呼、收礼物要说谢谢、还要给长辈让座。都是些小事，但它们变成了习惯。我记得我很害羞，所以父母会温和地提醒我开口说话。"},{"b":"02","t":10,"i":0,"en":"Yes, a few things. When I was a kid I loved making paper planes and little paper boats, and I once folded a whole box of paper cranes. I wasn't very good at it, but I enjoyed the process. It's a simple, cheap way to be creative.","cn":"做过几样。小时候我喜欢折纸飞机和纸船，还折过一整盒的千纸鹤。我做得不算好，但我享受这个过程。它是一种简单、便宜又能发挥创意的方式。"},{"b":"02","t":10,"i":1,"en":"Honestly, almost never now. It's all messages and emails these days — they're faster and more convenient. The last time I wrote a real letter was probably years ago. I do miss the personal touch of it, though.","cn":"说实话，现在几乎不写了。如今都是发消息和邮件——更快也更方便。我上次写真正的信大概是好几年前了。不过我确实怀念那种亲手书写的感觉。"},{"b":"02","t":10,"i":2,"en":"Some people do, but I think it's becoming rare. Handwritten letters feel much more personal and meaningful than a text, so people keep them as keepsakes. My grandmother still has letters from decades ago. But for everyday communication, most people have given up on paper.","cn":"有些人会，但我觉得越来越少了。手写信比短信更有个人色彩、也更有意义，所以人们会把它们当纪念留着。我奶奶还留着几十年前的信。但作为日常交流，大多数人已经不用纸了。"},{"b":"02","t":10,"i":3,"en":"Not usually, no. I used to carry a notebook everywhere, but now my phone covers almost everything — notes, lists, reminders. The only time I carry a pen is for exams, when we're not allowed to use phones. Otherwise it's just my phone.","cn":"一般不带。以前我到哪都带个本子，但现在手机几乎包办了一切——记笔记、列清单、设提醒。我唯一带笔的时候是考试，因为考试不让用手机。其他时候就只带手机。"},{"b":"02","t":10,"i":4,"en":"I used to love drawing on paper and making little cards for my family. I also covered my schoolbooks in paper to keep them clean. It was a fun, messy kind of play. These days, of course, kids just use tablets, which I think is a bit of a shame.","cn":"我以前很喜欢在纸上画画，还给家人做小卡片。我还会用纸把课本包起来防脏。那是一种又好玩又乱糟糟的玩法。当然，现在的孩子都用平板了，我觉得有点可惜。"},{"b":"02","t":11,"i":0,"en":"If I see a piece of rubbish on the street, I usually pick it up and drop it in the nearest bin. It's a small thing, but it keeps the place tidy. I think if everyone did that, the streets would look much better. I don't lecture people, though — that would be annoying.","cn":"如果在街上看到垃圾，我通常会捡起来扔进最近的垃圾桶。这是件小事，但能让环境整洁。我觉得如果每个人都这么做，街道会好看很多。不过我不会去教训别人——那会很烦人。"},{"b":"02","t":11,"i":1,"en":"I separate things at home before I throw them out. Paper and cardboard go in one bag, plastic bottles in another, and food waste in a third. Every building has four bins now, so it's pretty easy. I also rinse bottles before recycling, so they don't smell.","cn":"我在家扔之前会先分类。纸和纸板放一个袋子，塑料瓶放另一个，厨余放第三个。现在每栋楼都有四个桶，所以挺容易的。我还会在回收前冲洗瓶子，这样不会有味道。"},{"b":"02","t":11,"i":2,"en":"Yes, it's very common now. The four-bin rule came in about two years ago, and it's everywhere — homes, schools and offices. At first it confused people, but most of us are used to it now. I think it has made the city cleaner overall.","cn":"是的，现在很普遍。四个桶的规定大约两年前就推行了，到处都在用——家里、学校、办公室。一开始大家有点混乱，但现在大多数人都习惯了。我觉得它总体上让城市更干净了。"},{"b":"02","t":11,"i":3,"en":"Not really, no. When I was a kid, everything just went into one bin. Nobody sorted anything — we didn't think about it. So recycling is really a habit I learned as an adult, when the new rule came in. It took me a while to get used to it.","cn":"小时候其实没有。那时候所有东西都扔进一个桶。没人分类——我们也没想过这事。所以回收其实是我成年后、新规定推行时才学会的习惯。我花了一段时间才适应。"},{"b":"04","t":1,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I do. My favourite teacher was my English teacher in high school. She was strict but fair, and she always made the class interesting. What I liked most was that she treated us like adults, not kids. She's the reason I'm still interested in languages.","cn":"有的。我最喜欢的老师是高中英语老师。她严格但公正，总能把课上得很有意思。我最喜欢的是她把我们当成年人、而不是小孩对待。她就是我现在还喜欢语言的原因。"},{"b":"04","t":1,"i":1,"en":"Honestly, probably not as a full-time job. I respect teachers a lot, but I don't think I have the patience for a whole class. I do enjoy explaining things to others, though, so maybe tutoring one-on-one part-time would suit me. A classroom full of kids? Not for me.","cn":"说实话，大概不会当全职。我很尊敬老师，但我觉得自己对一整个班没那么有耐心。不过我确实喜欢给别人讲东西，所以一对一兼职做家教可能适合我。一屋子小孩？那不适合我。"},{"b":"04","t":1,"i":2,"en":"Yes, my primary school teacher, Miss Chen. She was very gentle and never shouted. When I was shy and afraid to speak, she would quietly encourage me instead of putting me on the spot. I still remember her warm smile, even though it was years ago.","cn":"有的，我的小学老师陈老师。她特别温和，从不吼人。我害羞、不敢说话时，她会悄悄鼓励我，而不是让我当众难堪。这么多年过去了，我至今还记得她温暖的笑容。"},{"b":"04","t":1,"i":3,"en":"Sadly, no. We lost touch after I moved to a different school for middle school. I sometimes think about going back to visit, but a lot of time has passed and I'm not sure she'd even remember me. It's a bit of a regret, actually.","cn":"很遗憾，没有了。我初中换学校之后我们就断了联系。我有时会想回去看看，但时间过去太久了，我也不确定她是否还记得我。其实有点遗憾。"},{"b":"04","t":1,"i":4,"en":"In a lot of ways. She helped me academically, of course, but more than that, she taught me to be confident. She once told me my writing was good, and that small comment stayed with me for years. Sometimes one kind teacher can change how you see yourself.","cn":"在很多方面。学业上她当然帮了我，但更重要的是，她教会了我自信。她曾说我写得好，这一句小小的评价我记了好多年。有时一个好老师就能改变你对自己的看法。"},{"b":"04","t":1,"i":5,"en":"Not more, exactly — differently. Primary teachers were more like parents, warm and gentle, because we were so small. High school teachers were stricter and pushed us harder, but that was because the exams were serious. I appreciate both for different reasons.","cn":"谈不上更喜欢——是不一样。小学老师更像父母，温暖亲切，因为我们太小了。高中老师更严格、也逼得更紧，但那是因为考试很严肃。两种老师我出于不同原因都感激。"},{"b":"04","t":2,"i":0,"en":"Yes, plenty. There's an old riverside area in my city with low grey buildings and narrow streets, some of them over a hundred years old. I walk through it sometimes. What I like is that they sit right next to modern towers, so you can see the whole history of the city in one view.","cn":"见过的，很多。我市有个老河畔片区，灰色矮楼、窄街道，有些都上百年了。我有时会從那儿走过。我喜欢的是它们就挨着现代高楼，一眼就能看到这座城市的历史。"},{"b":"04","t":2,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I strongly think we should, at least the ones with real history. They hold the city's memory and give it character — without them, every city would look the same. Of course, they need to be looked after and made safe, not just left to fall down. But knocking everything down for new shops would be a real loss.","cn":"我觉得应该，至少有真正历史的那些。它们承载着城市的记忆、也给了它性格——没有它们，每座城市都长一个样。当然，它们需要被维护、保证安全，而不是任其倒塌。但为了建新商场就把一切都推倒，是真的损失。"},{"b":"04","t":2,"i":2,"en":"An old building, actually, as long as it's been renovated. Old buildings often have thicker walls, higher ceilings and more character. The problem is they can be cold, damp and inconvenient. So in reality I'd want the charm of an old building with the comfort of a modern one — but if I had to choose one, modern is safer for daily life.","cn":"其实我会选老建筑，前提是翻修过。老房子墙更厚、层高更高、也更有味道。问题是它们可能又冷又潮、还不太方便。所以现实中我想要老房子的韵味加上新房的舒适——但如果只能选一个，为了日常生活，新的更稳妥。"},{"b":"04","t":2,"i":3,"en":"Yes — I'd love to see some of the old European cathedrals in person, like the ones I've only seen in photos. And closer to home, there's an ancient temple in the mountains near my city that I've never visited. I think standing in a very old building really makes you feel history, more than reading about it.","cn":"想。我特别想去亲眼看看那些只在照片里见过的欧洲老教堂。离家近一点的话，我市附近山里有一座古庙，我一直没去过。我觉得站在一栋很老的建筑里，能比读书更真切地感受到历史。"},{"b":"04","t":3,"i":0,"en":"I like all kinds, honestly, but I lean towards realistic dramas and a bit of thriller. I enjoy films that feel like real life, with believable characters. I'm not a huge fan of big action movies — too much noise and not enough story for me.","cn":"其实我各种都喜欢，但偏爱写实剧情片和一点悬疑。我喜欢那种贴近真实生活、人物可信的电影。大片动作片我不太感冒——对我来说太吵、故事又不够。"},{"b":"04","t":3,"i":1,"en":"Yes, quite often. As a kid I watched a lot of cartoons and family films with my parents at home. It was our weekend habit. I have warm memories of falling asleep on the sofa while a film played. It was more about being together than about the film itself.","cn":"是的，挺经常的。小时候我常和父母在家看动画片和家庭电影，那是我们的周末习惯。我有很温暖的回忆——躺在沙发上看着看着就睡着了。那更多是关乎一家人在一起，而不是电影本身。"},{"b":"04","t":3,"i":2,"en":"No, never. I was always with my parents or friends as a child. Going to the cinema alone feels like something I only started doing as a student, when I wanted to watch something my friends weren't interested in. As a kid it just wasn't a thing.","cn":"没有，从来没有。小时候我总是和父母或朋友一起去。一个人去电影院，我觉得是当学生以后才开始的，那时我想看朋友不感兴趣的电影。小时候根本没有这种事。"},{"b":"04","t":3,"i":3,"en":"Not as often as I'd like, but yes, every now and then. It takes planning — everyone's busy — but when we do go, it's always fun. We usually grab food afterwards and talk about the film, which is often the best part.","cn":"没有我希望的那么频繁，但偶尔会去。它需要安排时间——大家都忙——但真去的时候总很开心。我们通常看完去吃个东西、聊聊电影，那往往是最棒的部分。"},{"b":"04","t":3,"i":4,"en":"Yes, I think it's a great way. It gives you something to share — you watch together and then discuss it. It's better than just sitting around, because there's a built-in topic of conversation. The only downside is that you can't really talk during the film.","cn":"我觉得是个好方式。它让你们有共同的东西可以分享——一起看、然后讨论。比干坐着好，因为天然就有话题。唯一的缺点是，看电影时没法真的聊天。"},{"b":"04","t":3,"i":5,"en":"Probably once or twice a week, usually at home on my laptop. In the cinema, maybe once a month at most. It depends on how busy I am and whether there's a film worth seeing on a big screen.","cn":"大概一周一两次，通常在家用电脑看。去电影院的话，最多一个月一次。这取决于我有多忙，以及有没有值得上大银幕看的片子。"},{"b":"04","t":3,"i":6,"en":"Both have their place. At home it's comfortable, cheap and I can pause whenever I want. But for a film with big visuals, the cinema is unbeatable — the huge screen and the sound make it a real experience. So for quiet dramas, home; for big films, the cinema.","cn":"两种各有各的好。在家舒服、便宜，还能随时暂停。但如果是画面宏大的电影，影院无可替代——大银幕和音效让它成为一种真正的体验。所以安静的剧情片在家看，大片就去影院。"},{"b":"04","t":4,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I loved it. There was a small park near my home with a slide and some swings, and I went there almost every day after school. I'd run around until dinner time. It was where I made my first real friends, actually.","cn":"喜欢。我家附近有个小公园，有滑梯和秋千，放学后我几乎天天去。我会一直玩到晚饭时间。其实我在那儿交到了第一批真正的朋友。"},{"b":"04","t":4,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I still do, though for different reasons. As a kid it was all about playing; now it's more about relaxing — going for a walk, sitting on a bench, getting some fresh air. It's where I go when I need to clear my head after studying.","cn":"还喜欢，不过理由不一样了。小时候全是玩；现在更多是放松——散散步、坐坐长椅、透透气。学习之后需要理清思路时，我就去那儿。"},{"b":"04","t":4,"i":2,"en":"Yes, definitely. The parks in my city are quite crowded, and there are only a few big ones. More small neighbourhood parks would be great, because you'd have somewhere to go within a few minutes' walk. Green space really improves the quality of life.","cn":"当然希望。我市的公园挺挤的，大的也就那么几个。多一些小区里的小公园会很好，走几分钟就能到。绿地真的能提升生活质量。"},{"b":"04","t":4,"i":3,"en":"Yes, there's a big national park in the mountains a few hours from my city that I've never been to. I've seen photos, and it looks amazing — forests, lakes, clean air. I'd love to go camping there one day. Also, maybe some famous parks abroad, like the big one in New York.","cn":"想。离我市几小时车程的山里有个大国家公园，我一直没去过。我看过照片，特别美——森林、湖泊、清新的空气。我想有一天去那儿露营。还有，也许国外一些有名的公园，比如纽约那个大公园。"},{"b":"04","t":4,"i":4,"en":"A public park, I think. A personal garden sounds lovely, but it's expensive and you'd have to look after it all by yourself. In a public park, there's more space, more people and a livelier atmosphere. You get the benefits without the work.","cn":"我会选公共公园。私人花园听起来很美，但很贵，还得全靠自己打理。公共公园里空间更大、人更多、气氛更热闹。你能享受好处，又不用操心。"},{"b":"04","t":4,"i":5,"en":"They're a bit different. Modern parks have better equipment — proper playgrounds, sports areas and clean paths. The old ones I remember were simpler and more natural, just grass and a few trees. But honestly, as a kid, it didn't matter. I had fun in both.","cn":"有点不一样。现在的公园设施更好——有正经的游乐场、运动区、干净的步道。我记得的老公园更简单、更自然，就是草地和几棵树。不过说实话，对小孩来说这都不重要，两种我都玩得开心。"},{"b":"04","t":4,"i":6,"en":"Usually I just walk around and enjoy the green, then sit on a bench for a while. Sometimes I read or listen to a podcast. If it's a nice day I might fly a kite or play badminton with friends. The main thing is slowing down and being outside for a bit.","cn":"通常我就是走走、享受绿色，然后在长椅上坐一会儿。有时我看书或听播客。天气好的话，我可能和朋友放风筝、打羽毛球。主要是慢下来，在外面待一会儿。"},{"b":"04","t":4,"i":7,"en":"Sure, why not — a public one is fine. I'm not picky. A public garden has more people around, so it feels more social and fun. I'd happily play basketball or just hang out there on a weekend. The only thing I'd avoid is going when it's packed.","cn":"当然，公共的就行。我不挑。公共花园周围人更多，感觉更热闹、更好玩。周末我很乐意去那儿打篮球或就是待着。唯一我会避开的是人特别多的时候。"},{"b":"04","t":5,"i":0,"en":"Yes, several times. I've been to the city history museum and also to the one in the old riverside area, which is inside an old building. I find them interesting if the displays are well done, though big museums can be tiring if you try to see everything in one day.","cn":"去过几次。我去过市历史博物馆，还去过老河畔区那一个，它就在一栋老建筑里。如果展陈做得好，我觉得挺有意思的，不过大博物馆如果一天想全看完，会很累。"},{"b":"04","t":5,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I do, though I'm not an expert. I enjoy learning about how people used to live — what they ate, how they built things, why wars happened. I think history explains a lot about the present, so it's worth knowing even if it's not your main interest.","cn":"喜欢，虽然我不是专家。我喜欢了解过去的人怎么生活——吃什么、怎么盖房子、为什么打仗。我觉得历史能解释现在的很多事，所以就算不是你的主要兴趣，也值得了解。"},{"b":"04","t":5,"i":2,"en":"Probably a few weeks ago, when I was reading about the city I live in for a school project. Before that, I'd read a book about world history a few months earlier. So I read about it every now and then, not every day.","cn":"大概几周前，我为一个学校项目读关于我居住的这座城市的历史。再往前，几个月前我读过一本世界史的书。所以我时不时会读，而不是每天。"},{"b":"04","t":5,"i":3,"en":"Honestly, not really. As a kid I found it boring — all those dates and names felt meaningless. It was only later, when I started travelling and seeing old places, that it became interesting. So my interest in history grew with age, not the other way round.","cn":"说实话，小时候不太喜欢。那时觉得它无聊——那些年代和人名都没什么意义。是后来我开始旅行、看到老地方，它才变得有意思。所以我对历史的兴趣是随年龄增长的，而不是反过来。"},{"b":"04","t":6,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I use them every day. I put them on when I'm studying, commuting or out for a run. They help me focus and shut out the noise around me. Honestly, they've become a bit of an essential item for me, like my keys or wallet.","cn":"用，每天都用。学习、通勤或跑步时我都会戴上。它们帮我专注、把周围的噪音挡在外面。说实话，它们已经成了我的必需品，就像钥匙和钱包一样。"},{"b":"04","t":6,"i":1,"en":"I mainly use in-ear ones, the type that sit inside your ear. I also have a pair of over-ear headphones for when I'm at home — they sound better and are more comfortable for long sessions. For going out, the small in-ear ones are just more practical.","cn":"我主要用入耳式的。我还有一副头戴式的，在家时用——音质更好，长时间戴也更舒服。出门的话，小的入耳式更实用。"},{"b":"04","t":6,"i":2,"en":"Mostly when I'm studying alone or on public transport. At home I use them when I don't want to disturb my family. And when I run, they keep me motivated with music. So really, any time I want to block out noise but stay focused.","cn":"主要是一个人学习或在公共交通上时。在家时，当我不想打扰家人也会用。跑步时，音乐能给我动力。所以基本上，任何我想隔绝噪音、保持专注的时候都会用。"},{"b":"04","t":6,"i":3,"en":"Yes — when I'm with other people, definitely. If someone is talking to me or we're having a meal, I take them off, because it's rude to keep them on. I also avoid them when I'm crossing a busy road, because it's dangerous not to hear the traffic. Being aware matters more than convenience.","cn":"会——和别人在一起时肯定不用。如果有人在跟我说话，或者我们在吃饭，我就会摘下来，因为一直戴着不礼貌。过繁忙马路时我也会避开，因为听不到车是危险的。注意周围比方便更重要。"},{"b":"04","t":6,"i":4,"en":"I'd say it depends on the type and how long you wear them. The soft in-ear ones feel fine for an hour or two, but after that my ears get sore. Over-ear ones are more comfortable for long use. So overall, they're fine for short sessions, but not something I'd wear all day.","cn":"我觉得这取决于类型和戴多久。软的入耳式戴一两个小时还行，但之后耳朵就会疼。头戴式的长时间戴更舒服。所以总的来说，短时间戴没问题，但我不会一整天都戴。"},{"b":"04","t":7,"i":0,"en":"Honestly, not really. I always forget the punchline or mess up the order, so the joke falls flat. I can be funny in a casual conversation, but telling a proper joke on the spot? That's not my strength. I admire people who can do it naturally.","cn":"说实话不太行。我总是忘记笑点，或者把顺序搞乱，笑话就冷场了。闲聊时我能挺幽默，但现场讲一个正经笑话？那不是我的强项。我羡慕那些能自然讲出来的人。"},{"b":"04","t":7,"i":1,"en":"Yes, some of them do. I have one friend who's really good at it — he remembers every joke he's ever heard and tells them perfectly. It's actually a nice skill, because he can lighten up any awkward moment. I always laugh, even when I've heard the joke before.","cn":"有几个朋友是。我有个朋友特别擅长——他听过每个笑话都记得，还讲得特别好。这其实是个很棒的本事，因为他能化解任何尴尬的时刻。我总是会笑，哪怕这笑话我以前听过。"},{"b":"04","t":7,"i":2,"en":"Yes, I enjoy them, especially sitcoms. I like watching them when I want to switch off after a long day — they don't need much concentration, and they lift my mood. My favourite ones are the ones with clever writing, not just silly slapstick.","cn":"喜欢，尤其是情景喜剧。一天下来累了想放空时，我喜欢看——不用太费脑子，还能让心情变好。我最喜欢那种台词写得妙的，而不只是傻乎乎地搞笑。"},{"b":"04","t":7,"i":3,"en":"No, I've never been to a live comedy show. I'd like to, though — I imagine the atmosphere is completely different from watching on a screen, because the laughter is shared and there's a real connection with the performer. Maybe one day when I get the chance.","cn":"没有，我从来没去过现场的喜剧演出。不过我挺想去的——我想现场的气氛肯定和看屏幕完全不一样，因为笑声是共享的，和表演者之间也有真实的互动。也许哪天有机会就去。"},{"b":"04","t":7,"i":4,"en":"I think so, yes, especially online. Stand-up comedy has become really popular among young people, and there are lots of comedy shows and clips online. In traditional media, comedy is a bit more gentle and family-friendly. So there's plenty to choose from, depending on your taste.","cn":"我觉得挺流行的，尤其是网上。脱口秀在年轻人里变得很火，网上有很多喜剧节目和片段。传统媒体上的喜剧会更温和、更适合全家看。所以选择很多，看个人口味。"},{"b":"04","t":8,"i":0,"en":"I like simple, comfortable clothes — mostly T-shirts, jeans and trainers. I'm not into fancy fashion at all. If the material is soft and the fit is right, I'm happy. I'd rather feel relaxed all day than look stylish but uncomfortable.","cn":"我喜欢简单、舒服的衣服——主要是T恤、牛仔裤和运动鞋。我完全不喜欢花哨的时尚。只要面料软、版型合适，我就满意了。我宁愿一整天放松，也不想好看但不舒服。"},{"b":"04","t":8,"i":1,"en":"Comfortable and casual, definitely, for everyday life. I save the smarter clothes for special occasions like interviews or weddings. But I do think there's a time and a place for each — you wouldn't wear a tracksuit to a job interview, for example.","cn":"日常生活绝对选舒服休闲的。正式一点的衣服我留到面试、婚礼这类特殊场合。但我觉得两种各有各的场合——比如你不会穿运动服去面试。"},{"b":"04","t":8,"i":2,"en":"Yes, I basically live in them. They're comfortable, easy to match with anything and they work in almost any casual situation. I have quite a few, in different colours — plain ones for everyday and a couple with simple designs for when I want to look a bit nicer.","cn":"是，我基本上就穿T恤。它们舒服、好搭配、几乎任何休闲场合都合适。我有挺多件、不同颜色——纯色的日常穿，几件有简单图案的想要好看点时穿。"},{"b":"04","t":8,"i":3,"en":"Not really. I usually know what I like, so I'll grab something within a couple of minutes. The only time I take longer is for something special, like a wedding. For daily life I don't want to waste time standing in front of the wardrobe, so I keep my clothes simple.","cn":"不会。我通常知道自己喜欢什么，几分钟就挑好了。只有特殊情况我才会花久一点，比如参加婚礼。日常生活我不想浪费时间站在衣柜前，所以我的衣服都很简单。"},{"b":"04","t":8,"i":4,"en":"Yes, a bit. On weekdays I usually wear something smarter — a shirt or a neat jumper, because I might have classes or meetings. At weekends I go full casual — T-shirts, hoodies, old jeans. It's nice to have that switch, because it feels like the weekend too.","cn":"有一点。工作日我一般穿得正式一点——衬衫或整洁的毛衣，因为有课或会要开。周末我就完全休闲——T恤、卫衣、旧牛仔裤。这种切换挺好的，因为感觉就像周末了。"},{"b":"04","t":8,"i":5,"en":"I mostly go for dark, neutral colours — navy, grey, black and white. They're easy to match and they don't show stains. But I do have a few brighter pieces, like a green jacket, for days when I want to feel a bit more cheerful. So it depends on my mood.","cn":"我大多选深色和中性色——藏青、灰色、黑和白。它们好搭配、也不容易显脏。但我也有几件亮一点的，比如一件绿色外套，想要心情更明朗时就穿。所以这取决于我的心情。"},{"b":"04","t":9,"i":0,"en":"Yes, sometimes. I watch sports on TV when there's a big event, like the Olympics or the World Cup. I'm not someone who follows every match, but when a major game is on, I'll sit down and watch. It's relaxing, and it's fun to follow the drama.","cn":"有时会。有大比赛时我会看电视上的体育节目，比如奥运会或世界杯。我不是每场都追的人，但重要的比赛来的时候，我会坐下来看。它很放松，跟着看比赛的过程也很有意思。"},{"b":"04","t":9,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I prefer live games — there's something about watching it as it happens, with the crowd and the tension. Even on TV, a live match is more exciting than a recording, because you don't know the result. You share the nervous moments in real time.","cn":"喜欢，我更喜欢看直播。看它实时发生、有观众、有紧张感，就是不一样。哪怕在电视上，直播也比录播更刺激，因为你不知道结果。你能实时分享那些紧张的时刻。"},{"b":"04","t":9,"i":2,"en":"Usually with my dad, or sometimes with a couple of friends. Watching with others is much more fun, because you can react together — cheer, complain, argue about the referee. Alone it's fine, but a bit flat.","cn":"通常和我爸，有时和一两个朋友。和别人一起看有意思多了，因为可以一起反应——欢呼、抱怨、争论裁判。一个人看也行，但有点平淡。"},{"b":"04","t":9,"i":3,"en":"I'd like to watch more tennis, actually. I've got into it recently and I find it fascinating — it's as much mental as physical. And maybe some athletics too, like the sprint events. Fast, tense and dramatic. So more individual sports, I'd say.","cn":"其实我想多看网球。我最近迷上了，觉得它特别吸引人——它既是体力的，也是心理的较量。也许还有田径，比如短跑项目。快、紧张、有戏剧性。所以我会说，想多看个人项目。"},{"b":"04","t":9,"i":4,"en":"It depends. With a big match, watching with friends is great — the energy is higher and it's more social. But for something I really care about, I sometimes prefer to watch alone, because I get nervous and I like to concentrate. So: friends for fun, alone for the games that matter.","cn":"看情况。重要比赛时，和朋友一起看很棒——更有活力、也更有社交感。但对我特别在意的比赛，我有时更喜欢一个人看，因为我会紧张、想集中注意力。所以：图开心就朋友一起看，关键比赛就一个人看。"},{"b":"04","t":9,"i":5,"en":"Yes, once — I went to see a football match in a stadium a few years ago. The atmosphere was incredible, completely different from TV. You could feel the crowd, hear the chants, and the pitch looked so much bigger. I'd love to go again.","cn":"去过一次——几年前我去体育场看了一场足球赛。气氛特别震撼，和电视上完全不一样。你能感受到人群、听到呐喊，球场看起来也大得多。我很想再去一次。"},{"b":"04","t":10,"i":0,"en":"Mostly study and information websites, honestly. I use sites for English learning, and I read a lot of news and articles. I also visit a few video and shopping sites when I'm relaxing. So it's a mix of useful and entertaining.","cn":"说实话主要是学习和信息类网站。我用一些网站学英语，也读很多新闻和文章。放松时我也会逛逛视频和购物网站。所以是有用的和娱乐的混在一起。"},{"b":"04","t":10,"i":1,"en":"Probably a dictionary and learning site I use for English. It's simple, fast and free — I can look up words, hear the pronunciation and see example sentences. It's not glamorous, but I use it almost every day, so it's genuinely my favourite.","cn":"大概是我用来学英语的一个词典兼学习网站。它简单、快、免费——我能查词、听发音、看例句。它不花哨，但我几乎每天都用，所以它是真真正正我最喜欢的。"},{"b":"04","t":10,"i":2,"en":"Yes, they've become much cleaner and more mobile-friendly. A few years ago the pages were crowded with ads and hard to read on a phone. Now most good sites load faster and look better on a small screen. I think the competition from apps pushed them to improve.","cn":"有，它们变得干净多了，也更适合手机。几年前页面挤满了广告，在手机上也很难读。现在大多数好网站加载更快、在小屏上看起来也更好。我觉得是来自App的竞争逼着它们改进。"},{"b":"04","t":10,"i":3,"en":"I'd say news and social media sites are the most popular, along with video platforms. Almost everyone I know uses them daily. Shopping sites are huge too, especially during big sales. So the popular ones are the ones that cover news, entertainment and shopping.","cn":"我觉得新闻和社交媒体网站最流行，还有视频平台。我认识的人几乎每天都用。购物网站也很火，尤其大促的时候。所以流行的都是覆盖新闻、娱乐和购物的那些。"},{"b":"04","t":10,"i":4,"en":"It depends on what I need. For quick facts and breaking news, websites are better — they're fast and up to date. But for deep understanding, books win, because they're more organised and reliable. So: websites for speed, books for depth.","cn":"看我要什么。查快速的事实和突发新闻，网站更好——快、也最新。但想深入理解，书更胜一筹，因为它们更有条理、也更可靠。所以：要快就上网，要深度就读书。"},{"b":"04","t":10,"i":5,"en":"Yes, I'd love to. Nothing complicated — maybe a simple blog where I write about my studies and the books I read. I think it would help me organise my thoughts, and it might even help other students. The only problem is keeping it updated regularly.","cn":"想，我很想。不用复杂——也许就是个简单的博客，写写我的学习和读过的书。我觉得它能帮我整理思路，说不定还能帮到别的学生。唯一的难点是坚持定期更新。"},{"b":"04","t":10,"i":6,"en":"A lot, actually. I've learned study techniques from websites, like how to make better notes and how to plan my time. I've also picked up practical things — recipes, simple exercises and even how to fix small problems on my laptop. So websites have taught me both academic and everyday skills.","cn":"其实学到了很多。我从网站上学会了学习方法，比如怎么做更好的笔记、怎么规划时间。还学了些实用的东西——菜谱、简单的锻炼，甚至怎么修电脑上的小毛病。所以网站教会了我不论学业还是日常的技能。"},{"b":"04","t":11,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I did. My family didn't have a car when I was very small, so when we did travel by car — usually to visit relatives — it felt like a real treat. I'd sit by the window and watch everything go past. Looking back, those trips felt like little adventures.","cn":"有。我小时候家里没车，所以难得坐车出门时——通常是去看亲戚——感觉特别新鲜。我会坐在窗边看一路的风景。回想起来，那些旅途就像小小冒险。"},{"b":"04","t":11,"i":1,"en":"I like practical, reliable cars more than flashy ones — something safe and comfortable. I'm quite drawn to small electric cars these days, actually. They're quiet, cheap to run and better for the environment. Looks matter a bit, but I care more about whether it does the job well.","cn":"比起花哨的，我更喜欢实用可靠的车——安全、舒服的那种。其实我最近挺喜欢小型电动车。它们安静、用车成本低、也更环保。外观有点重要，但我更在意它能不能把活干好。"},{"b":"04","t":11,"i":2,"en":"A passenger, honestly. I find driving quite stressful, especially in heavy traffic or when I don't know the route. As a passenger, I can relax, look out of the window or chat. Maybe when I'm more experienced I'll enjoy driving, but for now, I'm happy in the passenger seat.","cn":"说实话，我喜欢当乘客。我觉得开车压力挺大的，尤其堵车或路不熟的时候。当乘客我能放松、看风景或者聊天。等我更熟练了也许会喜欢开车，但现在，我就乐意当乘客。"},{"b":"04","t":11,"i":3,"en":"If I'm a passenger, I just relax or chat. If I'm driving, I try to stay calm and be patient — getting annoyed doesn't make the traffic move any faster. I might put on some music or a podcast to pass the time. The key is accepting that you can't control it.","cn":"如果我是乘客，我就放松或者聊天。如果是开车，我尽量保持冷静、有耐心——烦躁也不会让车流变快。我可能会放点音乐或播客打发时间。关键是接受你控制不了它。"},{"b":"04","t":11,"i":4,"en":"I'd say they're important, but not the most important thing. Colour affects how a car looks and how easy it is to keep clean — dark colours hide dirt, light ones look fresh. But I'd never choose a car just for its colour. It's more of a nice bonus.","cn":"我觉得挺重要的，但不是最重要的。颜色影响车的外观，也影响好不好打理——深色藏脏，浅色显干净。但我绝不会仅凭颜色选车。它更像是个加分项。"},{"b":"04","t":11,"i":5,"en":"Probably not, honestly. I'd rather spend that money on travel, a place to live or savings. A car just needs to be safe, reliable and comfortable — it doesn't have to be expensive to do that. So a good, sensible car would suit me better than a luxury one.","cn":"说实话大概不会。我宁愿把钱花在旅行、住房或存起来上。车只要安全、可靠、舒服就行——做到这些并不需要很贵。所以一辆好用的、理性的车比豪车更适合我。"},{"b":"04","t":12,"i":0,"en":"Not really, no. I used to wear one when I was younger, but these days I just check the time on my phone. My phone does everything — time, alarms, fitness tracking — so a watch feels a bit unnecessary for me. I do like how they look, though.","cn":"其实不太戴。我年轻时戴过，但现在我就用手机看时间。手机什么都包了——时间、闹钟、计步——所以手表对我来说有点多余。不过我确实喜欢它们的样子。"},{"b":"04","t":12,"i":1,"en":"Yes, once — a simple watch from my parents on my birthday. It wasn't expensive, but I wore it for years. I think when someone gives you a watch, it's often a message about time being precious. That's why it meant a lot to me.","cn":"收到过一次——生日时父母送的一块简单的手表。它不贵，但我戴了好多年。我觉得别人送你手表，常常是在传递'时间宝贵'的意味。所以它对我意义很大。"},{"b":"04","t":12,"i":2,"en":"I think for many people it's a symbol of success or status — like a small piece of luxury you can wear every day. Some see it as an investment that holds its value. And for others, it's just personal taste or a gift with meaning. So it's a mix of image and feeling.","cn":"我觉得对很多人来说，它是成功或身份的象征——一件能天天戴的小奢侈品。有些人把它看成能保值的投资。对另一些人来说，纯粹是个人品味或者一份有意义的礼物。所以里面既有形象，也有情感。"},{"b":"04","t":12,"i":3,"en":"For most people today, no, it's not essential — a phone does the job. But I do think a watch has value beyond telling time. A nice one is more like an accessory, and it can be a meaningful gift. So it's not necessary, but it can be meaningful.","cn":"对今天的大多数人来说，不，它不是必需品——手机就够了。但我觉得手表的价值不止于看时间。一块好表更像配饰，也可以是份有意义的礼物。所以它不是必需的，但可以有意义。"},{"b":"04","t":13,"i":0,"en":"I wouldn't say I love it, but I do look when I'm getting ready in the morning or before going out — mostly to check that my hair isn't a mess. So maybe a few times a day, not for long. I'm not someone who stares at themselves, honestly.","cn":"不能说很喜欢，但早上准备或者出门前我会看一眼——主要是确认头发没乱。所以一天大概几次，不会很久。说实话我不是那种盯着自己看的人。"},{"b":"04","t":13,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I have — a couple of small ones for the bathroom and bedroom. Nothing fancy, just practical. I bought them when I moved into my current place, because you don't realise how much you use a mirror until you don't have one. It was a boring but necessary purchase.","cn":"买过——浴室和卧室各一面小的。不花哨，就是实用。我搬进现在住的地方时买的，因为你会发现，没有镜子你才知道自己用得多。是笔无聊但必要的开销。"},{"b":"04","t":13,"i":2,"en":"No, not usually. I've never carried a small mirror in my bag. If I need to check something, I'll use my phone's front camera instead — it does the same job and it's already in my pocket. So I've never felt the need to carry one.","cn":"不，一般不。我从没在包里带过小镜子。如果需要看看，我会用手机前置摄像头——效果一样，而且本来就在口袋里。所以我一直没觉得需要带。"},{"b":"04","t":13,"i":3,"en":"Maybe, yes — a big one could look nice on a wall and make a room feel brighter. It's a cheap way to add light and space, especially in a small room. But I'd keep it simple and clean, not go overboard. A few well-placed mirrors, not a hall of them.","cn":"也许可以——一面大镜子挂在墙上会很好看，也能让房间感觉更亮。它是增加光线和空间感的便宜办法，尤其在小房间里。但我会保持简单干净，不会过头。几面放得巧的镜子，而不是满墙都是。"},{"b":"04","t":14,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I have, but not very often. I sometimes post photos when I travel or when something nice happens — a sunset, a good meal, a day out with friends. I'm quite private, though, so I don't share my daily life the way some people do. Maybe once or twice a month.","cn":"发过，但不频繁。有时旅行或者遇到好事我会发照片——日落、好吃的、和朋友出去玩。不过我比较注重隐私，不会像有些人那样分享日常。大概一个月一两次。"},{"b":"04","t":14,"i":1,"en":"I started in middle school, so quite a few years ago now. At first everyone was just sharing photos and chatting. It's changed a lot since then — now there's short video, live streaming and shopping. So I've watched it grow from simple sharing to a whole world.","cn":"初中开始的，所以到现在有好几年了。一开始大家只是发照片、聊天。从那以后变化很大——现在有短视频、直播、购物。所以我算是看着它从简单的分享长成一个完整的世界。"},{"b":"04","t":14,"i":2,"en":"Honestly, yes, sometimes. It's easy to open an app just to check something and then lose half an hour without noticing. I've started setting limits on my phone, and I try to keep it out of the bedroom at night. It's a work in progress, but I'm more aware of it now.","cn":"说实话有时候是的。很容易就想打开App看一眼，然后不知不觉半小时就没了。我开始给手机设使用限制，晚上也尽量把它放在卧室外。还在改的过程中，但我现在更有意识了。"},{"b":"04","t":14,"i":3,"en":"Yes, most of them do. It's become pretty much the norm for my generation. People use it for different things — some post a lot, some just follow others, and some mainly use the chat functions. So even if people are on it, they use it in very different ways.","cn":"是的，大多数都用。它对我们这代人来说几乎是常态了。人们用途不同——有的发很多，有的只看别人，有的主要用聊天功能。所以就算都在用，用法也很不一样。"},{"b":"04","t":14,"i":4,"en":"A lot of things, really. People share photos and short videos, follow news and hobbies, chat with friends, and increasingly, watch live streams or even shop. Some also use it to show off or seek attention. So it's a bit of everything — social, entertaining and, lately, commercial.","cn":"挺多的。人们发照片和短视频、关注新闻和爱好、和朋友聊天，现在越来越多的人看直播、甚至购物。有些人还用它炫耀或寻求关注。所以它是杂七杂八的——社交的、娱乐的，最近还是商业的。"},{"b":"04","t":15,"i":0,"en":"It depends on my mood, honestly. I like happy, upbeat music when I need energy or I'm doing housework. But I also enjoy sad songs when I want to feel something deeper — sometimes a sad song matches how you feel, and that's comforting rather than upsetting.","cn":"说实话看心情。我需要能量或者做家务时喜欢欢快、有活力的音乐。但想感受更深的东西时，我也享受悲伤的歌——有时候一首悲伤的歌和你的情绪很合拍，那是种安慰，而不是让人难过。"},{"b":"04","t":15,"i":1,"en":"Yes, definitely. Happy music lifts my mood and gives me energy — I move faster, feel lighter and it's easier to get things done. If I'm tired or a bit down, the right upbeat song can genuinely change my whole day. It's like a small reset button.","cn":"当然。欢快的音乐能提振情绪、给我能量——我会动作更快、感觉更轻松，事情也更容易做完。如果我累了或有点低落，一首合适的欢快歌曲真的能改变我一整天。就像一个小的重启键。"},{"b":"04","t":15,"i":2,"en":"No, I never have. I learned a little bit at school, like basic music theory, but I've never taken proper lessons or learned an instrument seriously. I sometimes wish I had — it seems like a skill that stays with you for life. Maybe it's not too late to start.","cn":"没有，从来没上过。我在学校学过一点，比如基础乐理，但从没正经上过课或认真学过乐器。我有时会希望自己学过——它像是一项能伴你一生的技能。也许现在开始也不晚。"},{"b":"04","t":15,"i":3,"en":"Yes, quite often. I usually listen while commuting, running or doing simple chores — things that don't need much concentration. But when I'm studying, I can't, because music distracts me, especially if there are words. So it depends on the task.","cn":"经常。我通常通勤、跑步或做简单的家务时听——这些不需要太专注。但学习时我不能听，因为音乐让我分心，尤其是有歌词的。所以这取决于做什么事。"},{"b":"04","t":16,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I do, though I'm not an expert. I enjoy looking at art — paintings, photography, even design. I think art is a way of seeing the world through someone else's eyes, and that's what draws me in. I don't need to understand every piece to enjoy it.","cn":"喜欢，虽然我不是专家。我喜欢看艺术——绘画、摄影，甚至设计。我觉得艺术是用别人的眼睛看世界的一种方式，吸引我的正是这一点。我不需要理解每件作品才能欣赏它。"},{"b":"04","t":16,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I do, now and then. I like the quieter galleries more than the big crowded ones, because you can actually take your time. My favourite visit was a small photography exhibition in an old building — it felt personal, and the photos told a real story.","cn":"会去，偶尔。比起又大又挤的，我更喜欢安静些的画廊，因为你能真正慢慢看。我最喜欢的一次参观，是老建筑里一个小型摄影展——感觉很个人，照片也在讲一个真实的故事。"},{"b":"04","t":16,"i":2,"en":"No, I don't think so. I enjoy art, but I don't have the talent or the drive to create it professionally. I'm more of an appreciator than a creator. That said, I'd love to improve my photography as a hobby — that's the closest I'd get to being an artist.","cn":"我觉得不会。我喜欢艺术，但我没有专业创作的天赋或动力。我更像是欣赏者，而不是创作者。话虽如此，我很想把摄影作为爱好提升一下——那是我最接近当艺术家的事了。"},{"b":"04","t":16,"i":3,"en":"I like both, but I lean towards traditional art if I had to choose. Old paintings have a kind of craft and patience that I really admire — you can feel the hours in them. Modern art can be exciting and clever, but sometimes I look at it and think, honestly, I could have done that. So traditional edges it for me.","cn":"两种都喜欢，但非要选的话我更偏向传统艺术。老画作有一种我很敬佩的匠心和耐心——你能感受到里面的时间。现代艺术可以很激动人心、很聪明，但有时我看完会想，说实话这个我也能做出来。所以传统艺术略胜一筹。"},{"b":"04","t":17,"i":0,"en":"Yes, a bit. I learned about the solar system and stars at school, and I've watched a few documentaries since. I find it fascinating but also a bit mind-bending — when you think about how huge space is, it makes everyday problems feel very small. So I know the basics, not much more.","cn":"学过一点。我在学校学过太阳系和星星，后来也看过几部纪录片。我觉得它很迷人，但也有点烧脑——你想想太空有多大，日常的烦恼就显得特别小。所以我懂些基础的，仅此而已。"},{"b":"04","t":17,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I enjoy them, when they're done well. I like the ones that explore big ideas — time, space, what's out there — rather than just explosions. Good sci-fi makes you think about being human, and that's what stays with me. Bad sci-fi is just noise.","cn":"喜欢，前提是拍得好。我喜欢那种探讨大概念的——时间、太空、外面有什么——而不只是爆炸。好的科幻会让你思考'何为人'，这才是留在我心里的。烂科幻就只是吵。"},{"b":"04","t":17,"i":2,"en":"Yes, I'd love to know more. The more I learn, the more questions I have — like how the universe started, whether there's life elsewhere. I don't need to be an expert, but I'd like a better understanding of it. It puts everything else in perspective.","cn":"想，我很想多了解。我学得越多，问题就越多——比如宇宙怎么来的、别处有没有生命。我不需要成为专家，但我想理解得更好一些。它能让你把其他一切看得更淡。"},{"b":"04","t":17,"i":3,"en":"Honestly, probably not. It sounds amazing, but I get nervous about flying, and a rocket is a hundred times more intense. Plus, it's dangerous. I'd much rather explore space from the ground, through telescopes and documentaries, and keep my feet safely on Earth.","cn":"说实话大概不会。听起来很棒，但我坐飞机都紧张，火箭要强烈一百倍。再加上还有危险。我宁愿在地面上探索太空——用望远镜和纪录片，把脚稳稳地留在地球上。"},{"b":"04","t":18,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I do, in a general way. I'm not a scientist, but I'm curious about how things work — the weather, the human body, technology. I think science is basically organised curiosity, and I like that attitude. It's less about facts and more about asking good questions.","cn":"喜欢，比较宽泛地喜欢。我不是科学家，但我对事物怎么运作很好奇——天气、人体、技术。我觉得科学本质上是有条理的好奇心，我喜欢这种态度。它更关乎提出好问题，而不只是记住事实。"},{"b":"04","t":18,"i":1,"en":"I started at primary school, like everyone, with simple things — plants, magnets, the water cycle. But I only really got interested in middle school, when we did experiments. Seeing something happen with your own hands is very different from reading about it in a book.","cn":"和大家一样，从小学开始的，学些简单的东西——植物、磁铁、水循环。但真正让我感兴趣的其实是初中做实验的时候。亲眼看着一件事发生，和从书里读到，是非常不一样的。"},{"b":"04","t":18,"i":2,"en":"Biology, I'd say. I find living things fascinating — how the heart works, how the brain stores memories, how plants turn light into food. It's about us, in a way, so it feels closer to daily life. Physics is impressive but harder for me to picture.","cn":"我会说是生物。我觉得生命很迷人——心脏怎么运作、大脑怎么储存记忆、植物怎么把光变成食物。它某种程度是关于我们自己的，所以感觉离日常生活更近。物理很厉害，但我更难想象。"},{"b":"04","t":18,"i":3,"en":"Mainly experiments at school — building simple circuits, growing plants under different conditions, testing what makes bread rise. Nothing groundbreaking, but it made ideas real. I also once fixed my laptop's overheating problem by learning about airflow online. So science shows up in everyday life.","cn":"主要是学校的实验——做简单电路、在不同条件下种植物、测试什么让面包发起来。没什么惊天动地的，但它让概念变得真实。我还曾通过在网上了解散热，修好了笔记本过热的问题。所以科学生活中处处都有。"},{"b":"04","t":18,"i":4,"en":"Not often, but occasionally. I'll watch a good documentary about space, nature or the human body now and then. I don't like the ones that are too technical or too dumbed down — the best ones explain clearly without making you feel stupid. A few a month is about right.","cn":"不常看，但偶尔会。我会时不时看一部关于太空、自然或人体的好纪录片。我不喜欢太技术化或者太弱智化（把观众当傻子）的——最好的那些既讲得清楚，又不会让你觉得自己很笨。一个月几部差不多。"},{"b":"04","t":18,"i":5,"en":"Yes, I think quite a lot do, especially families. Science museums are popular with kids and parents, and schools often organise trips there. They've also become more modern — lots of hands-on exhibits now, not just glass cases. So they're seen as fun and educational at the same time.","cn":"我觉得挺多的，尤其是有孩子的家庭。科技馆很受孩子和家长欢迎，学校也常组织去那儿。而且它们变得更现代了——现在有很多能动手的展项，而不只是玻璃柜。所以它们被看作既好玩又能学东西的地方。"},{"b":"04","t":19,"i":0,"en":"The evening, definitely. I'm not a morning person at all — it takes me a while to wake up and feel human. In the evening I'm calmer and more relaxed, and I can enjoy quiet time after the busy part of the day is done. So evenings suit me much better.","cn":"绝对是晚上。我完全不是早起型的人——我得花一会儿才能醒过来、像个人。晚上我更平静、更放松，可以在一整天忙完之后享受安静的时光。所以晚上更适合我。"},{"b":"04","t":19,"i":1,"en":"Usually I have dinner, take a short walk if the weather is nice, and then study or read for a while. Before bed I stop looking at screens so I can sleep well. It's simple, but I like the routine — it's my quiet time to unwind.","cn":"通常我吃晚饭，天气好的话散会儿步，然后学一会儿或看会儿书。睡前我会不看屏幕，这样能睡得好。很简单，但我喜欢这套固定的流程——那是我安静放松的时间。"},{"b":"04","t":19,"i":2,"en":"As a child, I usually did homework and then watched cartoons before bed. It was very different — no phone, no stress, just family time. My mum would read me a story sometimes. Looking back, evenings felt slower and warmer than they do now.","cn":"小时候，我通常先做作业，然后睡前看动画片。那时候很不一样——没有手机、没有压力，就是和家人在一起。我妈有时会给我读故事。回想起来，那时的晚上比现在更慢、更温暖。"},{"b":"04","t":19,"i":3,"en":"Because kids have a simple, fixed routine, and that's comforting. Everything happened at the same time every day — dinner, homework, a bit of TV, bed. As an adult, evenings are less certain and often busier, so I miss that predictability. It's part of why childhood feels safe in memory.","cn":"因为小孩有简单固定的流程，那让人安心。所有事每天都在同一个时间发生——晚饭、作业、看会儿电视、睡觉。作为成年人，晚上没那么确定、也常常更忙，所以我怀念那种规律。这也是童年在记忆里显得安全的原因之一。"},{"b":"04","t":19,"i":4,"en":"I hate doing anything stressful in the evening, like dealing with problems or difficult conversations. It keeps me awake and ruins my rest. I also try to avoid heavy studying late at night — I've learned that anything important is better done in the morning. Evenings should be for winding down, not winding up.","cn":"我讨厌在晚上做任何有压力的事，比如处理麻烦或者困难的谈话。它会让我睡不着、毁了休息。我也尽量避免深夜重度学习——我发现重要的事早上做更好。晚上应该用来放松，而不是让自己紧张起来。"},{"b":"04","t":20,"i":0,"en":"The first thing I do is drink a glass of water and open the window for some fresh air. Then I wash my face and get dressed. I try not to check my phone straight away, because if I do, I get sucked into messages and lose time. So water and air first, phone later.","cn":"我做的第一件事是喝一杯水、开窗透气。然后洗脸、穿衣服。我尽量不一起来就看手机，因为一看就会被消息吸进去、浪费时间。所以先喝水透气，手机放后面。"},{"b":"04","t":20,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I think it's very important. It gives you energy for the morning and stops you snacking later. When I skip breakfast, I feel slow and hungry by ten. I don't need anything fancy — even a bit of fruit and some bread makes a real difference to how I feel.","cn":"我觉得非常重要。它给你上午的能量、还能防止你后面乱吃零食。我不吃早饭的话，十点就又困又饿。我不需要多丰盛——哪怕一点水果加面包，对我的状态影响都很大。"},{"b":"04","t":20,"i":2,"en":"It's pretty simple. I get up at six, run for about thirty minutes, then stretch and have breakfast. I plan three main tasks for the day while I eat. I keep it fixed, so I don't waste time deciding things. The whole thing takes about an hour, but it sets up the whole day.","cn":"挺简单的。我六点起床，跑大约三十分钟，然后拉伸、吃早饭。吃的时候我会规划当天三个主要任务。我会把它固定下来，这样就不用花时间做决定。整套下来大概一小时，但它定下了整天的基调。"},{"b":"04","t":20,"i":3,"en":"Yes, I actually love it now, though I didn't at first. Getting up early gives me a calm, quiet hour before the day gets busy, and the streets are empty and peaceful. It took me about two weeks to get used to it. Now if I sleep in, I feel like I've missed something good.","cn":"其实我现在很喜欢，虽然一开始不是。早起给我一天变忙之前一个平静、安静的小时，街上空空的、很安宁。我花了两周才适应。现在如果我睡懒觉，会觉得错过了什么好东西。"},{"b":"04","t":21,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I do, but only when I actually need something. I'm not the type to shop for fun or wander around for hours. I enjoy it more when I have a clear goal — like finding a good pair of shoes — and I can take my time. Aimless browsing is not for me.","cn":"喜欢，但只在我真需要东西的时候。我不是那种为了好玩逛街、一逛几小时的人。有明确目标时我更享受——比如找一双好鞋——我可以慢慢挑。漫无目的地逛不是我的菜。"},{"b":"04","t":21,"i":1,"en":"Maybe once every couple of weeks for clothes or shoes, and more often for small things like food and daily items. So it's not a big hobby, more a regular errand. Big shopping trips are rare for me — I buy when things wear out.","cn":"买衣服鞋子大概两周一次，食品和日用品这类小东西更频繁。所以它不算大爱好，更像日常事务。对我来说大采购很少——东西用坏了才买。"},{"b":"04","t":21,"i":2,"en":"Both, depending on what I'm buying. For clothes I still prefer in-store, because I want to try them on and feel the material. For books, electronics or daily items, online is much easier and often cheaper. So it's a mix — try in person, bulk-buy online.","cn":"两种都用，看买什么。买衣服我还是更喜欢实体店，因为想试穿、摸材质。买书、电子产品或日用品，网上方便多了、也常常更便宜。所以是混着来——试穿去实体店，囤货上网。"},{"b":"04","t":21,"i":3,"en":"Yes, once — a pair of shoes that looked great online but were a size too small. The return process was actually easier than I expected; I just printed a label and dropped it off. It did make me more careful about checking sizes and reviews before buying again.","cn":"退过一次——一双网上看着很棒、但小了一码的鞋。退货流程其实比我想的容易；我打印了标签、寄回去就行。它确实让我之后买东西更注意核对尺码和评价。"},{"b":"04","t":22,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I do. I can't concentrate or relax in a messy space — it makes me feel unsettled. My desk is usually clear, and I put things back where they belong. I'm not obsessive about it, but a tidy room helps me think clearly. It's part of how I stay calm.","cn":"喜欢。在乱糟糟的环境里我没法专注、也没法放松——会让我烦躁。我的桌子一般很清爽，东西用完放回原位。我不是强迫症，但整洁的房间能让我思路清晰。这是我保持平静的一部分。"},{"b":"04","t":22,"i":1,"en":"Honestly, no, the opposite. As a kid my room was a disaster — clothes everywhere, books on the floor. My mum was always telling me to tidy up. I only became tidy later, when I realised how much better I studied in an organised space. So it's a habit I learned, not one I was born with.","cn":"说实话正相反。小时候我房间一团糟——衣服到处都是、书扔在地上。我妈总让我收拾。我是后来才变得整洁的，因为我发现整洁的空间里学习效率高得多。所以这是我学会的习惯，不是天生的。"},{"b":"04","t":22,"i":2,"en":"Simple rules help. Everything has a place, so I never have to think about where to put things. I clear my desk at the end of each day, so I start fresh in the morning. And I deal with paper and messages immediately instead of letting them pile up. Small habits, done consistently.","cn":"简单的规则有帮助。每样东西都有固定的位置，所以我不用想该放哪儿。每天结束我会清空桌子，第二天就能从干净的状态开始。纸张和消息我会立刻处理，而不是让它们堆积。小习惯，但一直坚持。"},{"b":"04","t":22,"i":3,"en":"I think some tidiness is necessary, yes, but not perfection. You don't need a spotless home, but a basic order helps you find things, saves time and reduces stress. Being too obsessive can be its own problem. So I'd say: tidy enough to function well, not so tidy that it controls you.","cn":"我觉得一定程度的整洁是必要的，但不追求完美。你不需要一尘不染的家，但基本的秩序能帮你找到东西、省时间、减轻压力。太强迫本身也是个问题。所以我会说：整洁到能高效生活就好，但别整洁到被它控制。"},{"b":"04","t":23,"i":0,"en":"Honestly, I wanted to be a pilot. I was obsessed with planes as a kid — I had model planes and books about them. I loved the idea of flying and seeing the world from above. Obviously that didn't happen, but the dream of travel and freedom kind of stayed with me in other forms.","cn":"说实话，我想当飞行员。小时候我特别迷飞机——有飞机模型，还有关于飞机的书。我喜欢飞行、从上面看世界的那种感觉。显然那没实现，但那种关于旅行和自由的梦想，以其他形式留在了我身上。"},{"b":"04","t":23,"i":1,"en":"Somewhat, yes. I don't give up easily once I decide something matters — like my morning run, I've kept it going for months. But I'm also realistic; if a dream clearly isn't working, I'd rather adjust it than waste years on it. So I stick to the goals that still make sense.","cn":"有一定程度是的。一旦我认定一件事重要，就不轻易放弃——比如晨跑，我坚持了好几个月。但我也很现实；如果一个梦想明显行不通，我宁愿调整它，也不愿在上面浪费几年。所以我坚持的是那些仍然合理的目标。"},{"b":"04","t":23,"i":2,"en":"I'd love to work in something international, maybe in education or media, where I use languages and meet people from different places. I don't need it to be glamorous — I'd rather have work that's meaningful and lets me keep learning. So something with people and ideas, not just paperwork.","cn":"我很想做某种国际化的工作，也许是教育或传媒，能用到语言、接触来自不同地方的人。我不需要它多光鲜——我更希望工作有意义、还能让我不断学习。所以是和人、和想法打交道的事，而不只是文书工作。"},{"b":"04","t":23,"i":3,"en":"I think I am, in a quiet way. I'm not the type to talk loudly about big plans, but I do set goals and work towards them step by step — like training for a longer run or improving my English. I'd call it steady ambition rather than flashy ambition. I want to grow, just at my own pace.","cn":"我觉得算是，比较低调的那种。我不是那种把大计划挂在嘴上的人，但我会定目标、然后一步步去实现——比如训练跑得更远，或者提高英语。我会叫它稳扎稳打的野心，而不是张扬的野心。我想成长，只是按自己的节奏。"},{"b":"04","t":24,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I love singing, even though I'm not particularly good at it. I sing in the shower, in the car, or when a song I love comes on. It just lifts my mood instantly. It's less about performing and more about feeling good. For me, singing is a kind of free therapy.","cn":"喜欢，虽然我唱得不算特别好。我在洗澡时、车上、或者听到喜欢的歌时都会唱。它能立刻让我心情变好。它更像是一种让自己开心的方式，而不是表演。对我来说，唱歌是一种免费的治疗。"},{"b":"04","t":24,"i":1,"en":"No, I've never had proper lessons. Everything I know is self-taught, just singing along to songs I like. I sometimes wish I'd learned properly, because I know technique matters. But honestly, for fun, singing along is enough for me. Maybe one day I'll take a class.","cn":"没有，我从没上过正经的课。我会的都是自学的，就是跟着喜欢的歌一起唱。我有时希望自己正经学过，因为我知道技巧很重要。但说实话，为了开心，跟着唱就够了。也许哪天我会去上一节课。"},{"b":"04","t":24,"i":2,"en":"Honestly, I'd sing for the people closest to me — my family and close friends. I'd feel too shy to sing in front of a crowd, but for people I trust, I'd happily sing, even if I'm off-key. For them, it's not about how well I sing, it's just fun.","cn":"说实话，我想唱给我最亲近的人听——家人和好朋友。在人前唱我会太害羞，但对信得过的人，我很乐意唱，哪怕跑调。对他们来说，重要的不是我唱得多好，就是图个乐。"},{"b":"04","t":24,"i":3,"en":"Yes, definitely. Whether you sing well or badly, it makes you feel something — it releases emotion and brings people together. Singing together, like at a party or a concert, creates a shared happiness you can't really get from anything else. Even a bad singer can feel great after a good sing.","cn":"当然能。不管你唱得好不好，它都能让你有所感受——它能释放情绪、把人聚在一起。一起唱歌，比如聚会或演唱会上，能创造出一种别的什么给不了的共同快乐。哪怕唱得不好的人，痛快唱一场之后也会感觉很好。"},{"b":"04","t":24,"i":4,"en":"Yes, I do, but I'm quite picky. I enjoy good singers a lot — a beautiful voice can give me goosebumps. But I also like raw, emotional singers, even if they're not technically perfect, because you can feel they mean it. So it's more about emotion than pure skill for me.","cn":"喜欢，但我挺挑的。我很享受好歌手——一副好嗓子能让我起鸡皮疙瘩。但我也喜欢那种原始、有情感的歌手，哪怕技术上不完美，因为你能感觉到他们是真心的。所以对我来说，情感比纯粹的技巧更重要。"},{"b":"04","t":24,"i":5,"en":"No, I've never taken a singing class, which is a bit of a shame really. I've thought about it a few times, but I always put it off. Maybe I worry I'll be embarrassed. But I like the idea of learning properly one day — it's never too late to start something you enjoy.","cn":"没有，我从来没上过唱歌课，其实有点可惜。我想过几次，但总是拖着。也许我是怕丢脸。不过我挺想哪天正经学一下——喜欢的事，什么时候开始都不晚。"},{"b":"06","t":1,"i":0,"en":"Some places are easier because they feel relaxed, like a café, a park or someone's home — you can talk without shouting. Others aren't suitable because they're too noisy, too formal or too crowded — like a busy station or a fancy restaurant. So it's really about whether you can talk comfortably and enjoy each other's company.","cn":"有些地方更合适，是因为它们让人放松，比如咖啡馆、公园或者家里——你可以不用喊就能聊天。有些不合适，是因为太吵、太正式或者太挤——比如繁忙的车站或高档餐厅。所以关键在于你能不能舒服地聊天、享受彼此的陪伴。"},{"b":"06","t":1,"i":1,"en":"I like both, but I lean towards one or two close friends. With a small group you can have a real conversation and actually listen to each other. A big group can be fun and lively, but you often only talk to the person next to you. So it depends on my mood, but deep talks need fewer people.","cn":"两种都喜欢，但我偏向一两个好朋友。人少你能真正聊天、真正听对方说话。一大群人也能很热闹，但往往只能和旁边的人说话。所以看心情，但深入的谈心需要人少。"},{"b":"06","t":1,"i":2,"en":"Yes, I would, and I do sometimes. Home is relaxed and cheap — no need to book anything or shout over noise. I'd cook something simple and just hang out. The only thing is that not everyone lives close by, so it's easier to meet somewhere in the middle.","cn":"会，有时也会。家里放松又省钱——不用预订、也不用盖过噪音喊话。我会做点简单的吃的，然后就待着。唯一的问题是大家住得不都近，所以约在中间的地方更方便。"},{"b":"06","t":1,"i":3,"en":"Very important — honestly, they're one of the best parts of my life. Friends are the people you can be yourself with, who support you when things are hard and celebrate with you when they're good. Studies and work matter, but friendships are what make life feel warm.","cn":"非常重要——说实话，他们是我生活中最好的部分之一。朋友是你可以做自己的人，在你困难时支持你、在你顺利时和你一起高兴。学习和工作重要，但友谊才是让生活有温度的东西。"},{"b":"06","t":1,"i":4,"en":"Yes, quite often. We usually meet at weekends, and sometimes for a quick meal on weekdays. It's not every day, because everyone's busy, but we keep in touch constantly online. So even when we can't meet, we're still close.","cn":"挺经常的。我们通常周末见，有时工作日也一起吃个饭。不是每天都见，因为大家都忙，但我们在网上一直保持联系。所以就算见不了面，关系还是近的。"},{"b":"06","t":1,"i":5,"en":"Usually at a café or a small restaurant, somewhere quiet enough to talk. Sometimes we meet at a park or go to someone's flat. We avoid busy places — the point is to talk, not just to be out. So comfortable and calm places win.","cn":"通常在咖啡馆或小餐馆，要安静到能说话的那种。有时我们约在公园，或者去谁家里。我们会避开人多的地方——重点是聊天，而不只是出门。所以舒服、安静的地方最受欢迎。"},{"b":"06","t":1,"i":6,"en":"Mainly we just talk and eat — that's the core of it. Sometimes we watch a film, play a board game, or go for a walk. Nothing fancy. I think with good friends, it doesn't matter what you do; even doing nothing feels fine because you're together.","cn":"主要是聊天和吃东西——这是核心。有时我们看电影、玩桌游，或者散步。没什么花哨的。我觉得和好朋友在一起，做什么都不重要；哪怕什么都不做也挺好，因为你们在一起。"},{"b":"06","t":1,"i":7,"en":"Yes, I do — I have a friend I've known since primary school, so that's over ten years now. We don't meet often, but when we do, it's like no time has passed. Long friendships are special because they've seen you grow up.","cn":"有——我有个朋友从小学就认识，到现在十几年了。我们不常常见，但一见面就像没过时间。长久的友谊很特别，因为他们看着你长大。"},{"b":"06","t":2,"i":0,"en":"Mostly fresh food, I'd say — fruit, vegetables, snacks and street food. People also buy cheap clothes, small household items and sometimes flowers. The point of a street market is that it's fresh, cheap and lively, so food is the main thing. You go for the atmosphere as much as the shopping.","cn":"我想主要是新鲜食物——水果、蔬菜、零食和小吃。人们也会买便宜的衣服、小件日用品，有时还有花。街头市场的意义就在于新鲜、便宜、热闹，所以食物是大头。你去那儿一半是为了气氛，一半才是买东西。"},{"b":"06","t":2,"i":1,"en":"Honestly, it depends. For fresh food, I prefer the street market — it's cheaper and the produce is often better. But for clothes, electronics or branded items, the mall is safer, because you get quality and can return things. So street market for food, mall for everything else.","cn":"说实话看情况。买新鲜食材，我更喜欢街头市场——更便宜，东西往往也更好。但买衣服、电子产品或有牌子的东西，商场更保险，因为有品质保证、还能退货。所以吃的去街头市场，其他去商场。"},{"b":"06","t":2,"i":2,"en":"Probably a couple of weeks ago, on a weekend morning. I went to buy fruit and some snacks, and just walked around for a bit. It was busy and noisy in a nice way — vendors calling out, people bargaining. I didn't buy much, but I enjoyed the atmosphere.","cn":"大概两周前，一个周末早上。我去买水果和一些零食，顺便逛了逛。它热闹嘈杂，但是那种让人舒服的热闹——小贩吆喝、人们砍价。我没买多少，但挺享受那种气氛的。"},{"b":"06","t":2,"i":3,"en":"Yes, very many. Almost every neighbourhood has one, and there are big ones in most cities. Some are daily, selling food; others are weekly, like a fair. They're part of everyday life here, especially for fresh produce. So yes, street markets are everywhere in China.","cn":"非常多。几乎每个街区都有一个，大多数城市还有大型的。有的是每天都有、卖吃的；有的是每周一次，像个集市。它们是我们日常生活的一部分，尤其是买新鲜食材。所以是的，中国到处都有街头市场。"},{"b":"06","t":3,"i":0,"en":"Not seriously, no. I don't have a proper collection like stamps or coins. But I do keep small things with meaning — tickets from trips, a few postcards, and photos. So it's more sentimental than a real hobby. I keep them in a box, not on display.","cn":"不算真正在收藏。我没有像邮票或硬币那样的正经收藏。但我会留一些有意义的小东西——旅行的票根、几张明信片、还有照片。所以与其说是爱好，不如说是念旧。我把它们放在盒子里，不摆出来。"},{"b":"06","t":3,"i":1,"en":"Yes, a few. I still have my old school notebooks, some toys and a couple of childhood photos. They're not worth anything, but they carry memories. Every now and then I look through them, and it's like a little time machine. So I keep them, even though they take up space.","cn":"有几样。我还留着旧课本、一些玩具和几张童年照片。它们不值钱，但承载着回忆。时不时翻一翻，就像一台小小的时光机。所以我留着它们，尽管它们占地方。"},{"b":"06","t":3,"i":2,"en":"Yes, if they mean something. I don't keep everything, but things tied to people and moments — a gift, an old letter, a ticket — I'd rather hold onto. They cost nothing to keep and bring back good feelings. So I'd say keep the meaningful old things, and let the rest go.","cn":"如果它们有意义，我会留。不是什么都要留，但和人和时刻相连的东西——一份礼物、一封旧信、一张票——我更愿意留着。它们不占什么成本，却能带回好的感受。所以我会说：有意义的老东西留着，其余的放手。"},{"b":"06","t":3,"i":3,"en":"I try to have a fixed place for everything. Everyday things like keys, wallet and headphones go in a small tray near the door. Papers and important documents go in one drawer. So when I need something, I don't have to search — I know where it should be. It saves a lot of time.","cn":"我尽量给每样东西固定一个地方。钥匙、钱包、耳机这类日常用品放在门口的一个小托盘里。纸张和重要文件放一个抽屉。所以需要时我不用到处找——我知道它该在哪。这能省很多时间。"},{"b":"06","t":4,"i":0,"en":"Both, honestly. For studying, writing and anything that needs a proper screen, I prefer a computer — it's faster and easier to concentrate. But for reading, watching videos or browsing in bed, a tablet is nicer, because it's light and comfortable to hold. So it depends on the task.","cn":"说实话两种都用。学习、写作和任何需要正经屏幕的事，我更喜欢电脑——更快、也更容易专注。但看书、看视频或者躺在床上浏览，平板更好，因为轻、拿着舒服。所以看做什么。"},{"b":"06","t":4,"i":1,"en":"I use a computer mainly for studying, writing and video calls. I use a tablet for lighter things — reading, watching films, or taking notes in class. So the rule for me is: computer for work that needs focus, tablet for casual use and reading. That's how I split it.","cn":"我用电脑主要是学习、写作和视频通话。平板用来做轻一点的事——看书、看剧、或者在课上记笔记。所以我的规则是：电脑做需要专注的活，平板用于休闲和阅读。我就是这么分工的。"},{"b":"06","t":4,"i":2,"en":"I think it was at primary school, in a computer class. We learned basic typing and simple programs. It felt like a big deal at the time — these huge old monitors. I wasn't allowed my own device until much later, so that first lesson really stuck with me.","cn":"我想是小学的电脑课上。我们学基础打字和简单的程序。那时候觉得是件大事——那些巨大的老式显示器。我很晚才被允许有自己设备，所以那第一节课真的让我印象深刻。"},{"b":"06","t":4,"i":3,"en":"Honestly, it would be much harder. Almost everything I do — studying, messaging, finding information, even banking — runs through a screen. Without them I'd have to do everything slowly, by hand or in person. I think we'd cope, humans always do, but life would be far less convenient and a lot slower.","cn":"说实话会难很多。我几乎做的每件事——学习、发消息、查资料、甚至银行业务——都通过屏幕进行。没有它们，我什么都得慢慢来，手工或者亲自去办。我觉得我们还是能应付，人类总能应付，但生活会远没有那么方便、也慢得多。"},{"b":"06","t":4,"i":4,"en":"Yes, in a few situations. When there's no Wi-Fi or the battery is dead, obviously. Also, when my eyes are tired or my back hurts, staring at a screen is hard. And when I'm outdoors or somewhere I should be present, I find it difficult and even rude to use a device. So often it's about the situation, not the machine.","cn":"有几种情况。没有Wi-Fi或者没电的时候，显然不行。还有眼睛累了、背疼的时候，盯着屏幕很难受。再就是在外、或者应该专注于当下的时候，我觉得用设备很难、甚至很不礼貌。所以常常是情境的问题，而不是机器的问题。"},{"b":"06","t":5,"i":0,"en":"Not often, no. I can usually find something to do or think about. But there are moments — like waiting for a long time, or a slow afternoon — when boredom creeps in. I think everyone feels bored sometimes; it's normal. The key is what you do with it.","cn":"不常觉得无聊。我通常能找到事做、或者想的事情。但有时候会有——比如等很久、或者一个很慢的下午——无聊就来了。我觉得每个人偶尔都会觉得无聊，这很正常。关键在于你拿它怎么办。"},{"b":"06","t":5,"i":1,"en":"Mostly when I'm stuck waiting — for a bus, an appointment, or someone who's late. Also in the late afternoon, when I've finished my main tasks but it's too early for dinner. And during long, repetitive tasks, my mind just drifts. So it's usually about waiting or repetition.","cn":"主要是我被卡在等待的时候——等公交、等预约、或者等人迟到。还有下午晚些时候，主要任务做完了，但离晚饭又太早。再就是做又长又重复的事情时，脑子就飘了。所以通常是关乎等待或重复。"},{"b":"06","t":5,"i":2,"en":"It depends. Sometimes I just let myself be bored for a bit — it's actually good for the brain, like a rest. Other times I reach for my phone, go for a walk, or find a small task. I try to turn it into something useful rather than endless scrolling, because scrolling makes me feel worse, not better.","cn":"看情况。有时我就让自己无聊一会儿——它其实对大脑有好处，像休息。其他时候我就拿手机、去散步，或者找点小事做。我尽量把它变成有用的事，而不是没完没了地刷屏，因为刷屏让我感觉更糟，而不是更好。"},{"b":"06","t":5,"i":3,"en":"I think childhood can be boring, but in a good way, and adulthood can be boring in a tiring way. As a kid, boredom leads to imagination — you invent games, you get creative. As an adult, boredom is often because of routine and chores, and it's harder to escape because you have responsibilities. So the boredom of childhood is lighter, and the boredom of adulthood is heavier.","cn":"我觉得童年可以无聊，但是好的那种无聊；成年也可以无聊，但是累的那种无聊。小孩的无聊会引向想象——你会自己发明游戏、变得有创意。成年人的无聊常常是因为例行的琐事，而且更难摆脱，因为你有责任。所以童年的无聊更轻，成年的无聊更重。"},{"b":"06","t":6,"i":0,"en":"If I find something someone lost, I'd try to return it. If there's an ID or a phone number inside, I'd contact the person directly or hand it to the nearest service desk. If it's cash or something valuable with no ID, I'd hand it to the police or building staff. The main thing is not to keep it — someone is probably worried.","cn":"如果我捡到别人丢的东西，我会想办法归还。如果里面有身份证或电话号码，我会直接联系本人，或者交给最近的服务台。如果是现金或没有身份信息的贵重物品，我会交给警察或物业。关键是不要自己留着——很可能有人正着急。"},{"b":"06","t":6,"i":1,"en":"Not every time, but for valuable things or things with ID, yes. If it's a wallet or phone, the police can help find the owner or keep it safe. For something small, like a scarf or a book, I'd hand it to the building or shop staff instead. So it depends on what it is — but honesty matters either way.","cn":"不是每次都报警，但贵重物品或带身份信息的会。如果是钱包或手机，警察能帮着找失主、或者妥善保管。如果是围巾、书这类小东西，我会交给物业或店员。所以看是什么东西——但不管怎样，诚实很重要。"},{"b":"06","t":6,"i":2,"en":"Yes, a few times, and it's always awful. I once lost my phone on a crowded street, and another time I left my umbrella everywhere. Losing something is that sinking feeling — your stomach drops and you replay the last hour in your head. So now I'm much more careful with my things.","cn":"丢过几次，每次都特别糟。有一次我在拥挤的街上丢了手机，还有一次我的伞到处都是。丢东西是那种心往下沉的感觉——胃里一沉，然后在脑子里回放过去一小时。所以现在我对自己的东西小心多了。"},{"b":"06","t":6,"i":3,"en":"Yes, I would — it's actually a smart move. Social media spreads fast, and people do return things when they see a post. I'd describe the item, the place and the time, but I'd leave out small details, so I can check that whoever finds it is the real owner. So yes, I'd post, but carefully.","cn":"会——这其实是个聪明的做法。社交媒体传播得快，人们看到帖子确实会归还。我会描述物品、地点和时间，但会略去一些小细节，这样我就能核实来找的人是不是真正的失主。所以我会发帖，但会谨慎。"},{"b":"06","t":6,"i":4,"en":"Yes, more than once — I'm embarrassed to say. Keys are the worst because they're small and easy to drop without noticing. The last time, I found them in my coat pocket, right where I'd been looking. So now I always put my keys in the same tray by the door, and I haven't lost them since.","cn":"丢过，不止一次——说起来有点不好意思。钥匙最糟，因为它们小、掉了也不容易察觉。上一次，我在外套口袋里找到了，就在我找过的地方。所以现在我都把钥匙放在门口固定的托盘里，从那以后就没丢过。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":0,"en":"In the future, I'd love a small flat in a quiet neighbourhood, ideally near a park or the river. I don't need anything big — two rooms would be enough. What matters most to me is natural light and a balcony, so I can sit outside and have some green around me. Comfort matters more than size.","cn":"将来我想要一套安静街区的小公寓，最好在公园或河边附近。不需要很大——两个房间就够了。对我来说最重要的是自然采光和阳台，这样我能坐在外面、周围有点绿色。舒适比面积更重要。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":1,"en":"Yes, pretty good. There's a metro station about ten minutes' walk away, and several bus lines stop nearby. It's easy to get to the city centre, and there's a bike-share point right outside. The only downside is that it can get busy during rush hour, but overall I can't complain.","cn":"挺好的。走路十分钟有个地铁站，附近还有几条公交线路。去市中心很方便，门口就有共享单车点。唯一不好的就是高峰期会挤，但总的来说我没什么可抱怨的。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":2,"en":"I prefer an apartment, honestly. Houses are lovely if you want space and a garden, but they're more work — repairs, cleaning, security. An apartment is easier to maintain and usually closer to the city. For my age and lifestyle right now, a flat makes much more sense.","cn":"说实话我更喜欢公寓。想要空间和花园的话，独栋房子很好，但更费事——维修、打扫、安全都得管。公寓更容易打理，通常也更靠近市区。以我现在的年龄和生活方式，公寓合理得多。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":3,"en":"My room is small but bright. There's a bed by the window, a desk with my laptop, and a bookshelf that's overflowing. I keep it fairly tidy — a few plants on the windowsill and photos on the wall. It's not fancy, but it's my own space, and I like it that way.","cn":"我的房间不大，但很亮。窗边有张床，一张放电脑的书桌，还有一个塞满了的书架。我保持得比较整洁——窗台上有几盆植物，墙上贴着照片。不华丽，但它是属于我自己的空间，我喜欢这样。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":4,"en":"My favourite part is the window area. It gets the morning sun, and I have a few plants and a little chair there. It's where I have my coffee, read, or just look outside for a break. That small spot makes the whole room feel warmer and calmer.","cn":"我最喜欢的部分是靠窗的地方。那里有早晨的阳光，我放了几盆植物和一把小椅子。我在那儿喝咖啡、看书，或者就是看看窗外休息一下。那一小块地方让整个房间都更温暖、更平静。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":5,"en":"I've lived here for about three years now, since I started university. Before that I lived with my parents in the same city. So it's my first place that's really my own, which is why I'm quite attached to it, even though it's small.","cn":"我在这儿住了大约三年了，从上大学开始。在那之前我和父母住在这座城市里。所以这是我第一个真正属于自己的地方，这也是为什么我挺喜欢它，尽管它很小。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":6,"en":"Probably not for a very long time, no. It's a good place for now, but I'd like to move at some point — maybe after I graduate, or if I find work in another area. So I see it as a temporary home, not a forever one. But I'll enjoy it while I'm here.","cn":"大概不会住很久。现在它是个好地方，但我想在某个时候搬走——也许毕业后，或者如果我在别的区找到工作。所以我把它当作一个临时的家，而不是永远的家。但待在这儿的时候我会好好享受。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":7,"en":"Sure. It's a small apartment in a fairly quiet street, on the third floor. There are shops, a market and a metro station within walking distance. The building is old but well kept, and there's a small courtyard with a few trees. Inside, it's simple and comfortable — bright, with wooden floors. It's nothing special, but it feels like home.","cn":"当然。它是一套小公寓，在一条挺安静的街上，三楼。走路范围内有商店、市场和一个地铁站。楼有点旧但维护得不错，还有个小院子、几棵树。里面很简单、很舒服——明亮，木地板。没什么特别的，但有家的感觉。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":8,"en":"The living room, definitely. That's where we eat, watch TV and talk. Even when everyone's busy, we drift back there in the evening. It's the centre of the flat — the room where everything happens. So that's where most of our time is spent.","cn":"绝对是客厅。我们在那儿吃饭、看电视、聊天。哪怕大家都忙，晚上还是会聚到那儿。它是这个家的中心——所有事都发生在那个房间。所以我们大部分时间都待在那儿。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":9,"en":"My bedroom, I'd say. It's the only place where I can fully relax and be alone. I can read, listen to music or just lie down without anyone disturbing me. It's a bit small, but that makes it cosy. So it's my little corner of peace.","cn":"我会说是我的卧室。那是唯一一个我能完全放松、独处的地方。我可以看书、听音乐，或者就躺着，没人打扰。它有点小，但反而更温馨。所以那是我小小的一片宁静之地。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":10,"en":"Small things, really. The morning light coming through the window, the plants on the sill, and knowing everything is where it should be. Also the smell of food cooking in the evening. It's not about expensive furniture — it's about feeling calm and safe, and being able to switch off.","cn":"其实都是小事。早晨透过窗户照进来的光、窗台上的植物，还有知道一切都在该在的地方。还有晚上做饭的香味。这跟昂贵的家具无关——而是关乎感到平静、安全，能真正放松下来。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":11,"en":"Yes, I think it's very important. Your home is where you rest and recharge, so if it's uncomfortable, everything else suffers — your mood, your sleep, even your work. It doesn't need to be big or fancy, but it should be a place where you can relax. A comfortable home quietly supports your whole life.","cn":"我觉得非常重要。家是你休息和充电的地方，如果它不舒服，其他一切都会受影响——你的心情、睡眠，甚至工作。它不需要大或华丽，但应该是个能让你放松的地方。一个舒适的家在默默支撑着你的整个生活。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":12,"en":"I live in an apartment, on the third floor of an old but well-kept building. It's not big, just a couple of rooms, but it's enough for me. I've been here since I started university, so it's the first place I've had on my own. I like that it's simple and quiet.","cn":"我住在一套公寓里，一栋维护得不错的老楼的三楼。不大，就几个房间，但对我来说够了。我从上大学起就住这儿，所以是我第一个属于自己的地方。我喜欢它简单、安静。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":13,"en":"I live with two flatmates, actually. We're all students, so sharing makes it cheaper and less lonely. We each have our own room but share the kitchen and living room. It's a good arrangement — we help each other out and there's always someone to talk to. But of course, we have to be considerate.","cn":"其实我和两个室友一起住。我们都是学生，合住更省钱、也没那么孤单。我们各有各的房间，但共用厨房和客厅。这是个不错的安排——我们互相帮忙，总有人可以聊天。当然，我们也得互相体谅。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":14,"en":"Mostly I study, cook, and relax. In the evening I might watch something or read. Weekends are for cleaning and catching up on sleep. So it's a normal, everyday rhythm — nothing dramatic. My flat is where I rest and get things done between classes.","cn":"主要就是学习、做饭、放松。晚上我可能看点什么或者看书。周末用来打扫和多睡一会儿。所以是很平常的日常节奏——没什么戏剧性的。我的公寓就是我在课间休息、把事情做完的地方。"},{"b":"08","t":1,"i":15,"en":"I live in a rented apartment in a student area of the city. It's a shared flat, so I have my own bedroom but share the common areas. It's affordable and close to everything I need, which is why I chose it. It's not luxurious, but it works well for student life.","cn":"我住在城市学生区的一套租来的公寓里。是合租房，所以我有自己的卧室，但共用公共区域。它租金不贵、离我需要的一切都近，这也是我选它的原因。它不豪华，但对学生生活来说很合适。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":0,"en":"My hometown is a city in the south of China, built along a river. It's not one of the huge cities, but it's definitely not a small town either — somewhere in the middle. It's known for its food and its old riverside area, which is why people like visiting.","cn":"我家乡是中国南方的一座城市，沿河而建。它不算那种超大城市，但也绝不是小镇——介于两者之间。它以美食和老河畔区闻名，所以人们喜欢去那儿玩。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":1,"en":"I'd say it's a medium-sized city. It has all the conveniences of a big city — malls, a metro, good hospitals — but it's still walkable and not overwhelming. You can get from one end to the other in about an hour. So it's big enough to be interesting, small enough to feel manageable.","cn":"我会说它是中等城市。它有大城市的所有便利——商场、地铁、好医院——但仍然适合步行、不会让人喘不过气。从这头到那头大概一个小时。所以它大到有意思，又小到能掌控。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":2,"en":"Sure. It's a riverside city with a long history. The old town by the river has narrow streets and low grey buildings, and it's where the city started hundreds of years ago. These days it's a mix — old neighbourhoods next to modern towers. The food is famous, especially the street snacks. And people are generally relaxed and friendly.","cn":"当然。它是一座有悠久历史的滨河城市。河边老城区有窄街道和灰色矮楼，几百年前城市就是从那儿开始的。如今它是新旧混合——老街区挨着现代高楼。它的美食很有名，尤其是街头小吃。而且人们总体来说很放松、很友善。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":3,"en":"I've lived there most of my life, so around twenty years, apart from now when I'm studying. So my whole childhood and most of my growing up happened there. It's the place I know best in the world — every street feels familiar.","cn":"我在那儿住了大半辈子，大概二十年，除了现在上学这段时间。所以我整个童年、大部分成长都在那儿。它是我在世界上最熟悉的地方——每条街都让我觉得亲切。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":4,"en":"Honestly, probably not for the rest of my life. I'd like to work in a bigger city or even abroad for a while, at least while I'm young. But I can see myself going back later, maybe when I want a calmer life. So it's home, but not necessarily my forever home.","cn":"说实话，大概不会一辈子住那儿。我想去更大的城市、甚至国外工作一段时间，至少趁年轻的时候。但我能想象自己以后回去，也许当我想过更平静的生活时。所以它是家，但不一定是我永远的家。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":5,"en":"Yes, I do — I'm quite fond of it. It's where my family and childhood friends are, and it's comfortable and familiar. It's not the most exciting city, but it has a good pace of life. Whenever I go back, I feel relaxed. So yes, I like it a lot, even if I might not live there forever.","cn":"喜欢——我挺喜欢它的。我的家人和童年朋友都在那儿，而且那儿舒服、熟悉。它不是最刺激的城市，但生活节奏很好。每次回去，我都觉得很放松。所以是的，我很喜欢它，哪怕我可能不会永远住在那儿。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":6,"en":"Yes, I do. Living there is easy and low-stress. The cost of living is reasonable, everything is close by, and people are friendly. The downside is that it can feel a bit limited if you want a bigger career or more variety. But for daily life and comfort, I really like living there.","cn":"喜欢。在那儿生活轻松、压力小。生活成本合理、什么都近、人也友善。缺点是如果你想有更大的事业或更多选择，可能会觉得它有点局限。但就日常生活和舒适度而言，我真的很喜欢住在那儿。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":7,"en":"What I like most is probably the river and the food. The riverside is beautiful, especially in the evening, and it's where everyone goes to walk and relax. And the food — the street snacks are amazing and cheap. Those two things give the city its character and its warmth.","cn":"我最喜欢的可能是那条河和美食。河边很美，尤其傍晚，是大家去散步放松的地方。还有食物——街头小吃好吃又便宜。这两样东西给了这座城市性格和温度。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":8,"en":"Yes, a couple of things. The traffic has gotten worse, and the air isn't always great because of the cars. Also, it can feel a bit slow and traditional sometimes — it's not the best place for certain new career paths. But these are minor compared to what I like about it.","cn":"有几处。交通变差了，而且因为车多，空气有时不太好。还有，它有时候感觉有点慢、有点传统——对某些新兴职业来说不是最好的地方。但和我喜欢它的地方比起来，这些都是小问题。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":9,"en":"It's most famous for its food, honestly — the street snacks and the local dishes bring in a lot of visitors. It's also known for its old riverside area and a bit of history. So people know it as a place to eat well and take a slow walk along the river.","cn":"说实话它最出名的是美食——街头小吃和本地菜吸引了很多游客。它也以老河畔区和一点历史出名。所以人们知道它是个能好好吃一顿、沿河慢慢走的地方。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":10,"en":"A little, yes. At school we learned some general history, but not much specifically about our own city. Most of what I know, I learned from my grandparents and from walking around the old town. So school gave me the basics; family and the city itself taught me the rest.","cn":"学了一点。学校里我们学了些通史，但关于本城的具体内容不多。我知道的大部分，是从爷爷奶奶那听来的，或者逛老城区时了解的。所以学校给了我基础，剩下的靠家人和城市本身。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":11,"en":"There are some, but I'd say fewer than in the big cities — a lot of young people move away for work. You see more older people in the neighbourhoods, and families with kids. So it's not empty of young people, but many of us leave after university. That's a common pattern here.","cn":"有一些，但我觉得比大城市少——很多年轻人为了工作搬走了。你在街区里看到的更多是老人和带孩子的家庭。所以不是没有年轻人，但我们很多人大学毕业后就离开了。这是个很常见的现象。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":12,"en":"Not really, I'd say honestly. It's a good place to grow up and to live comfortably, but for ambitious careers, young people often need to go to the bigger cities. The opportunities are more limited here. So I'd call it a good place to live, but not the best place to launch a career.","cn":"说实话不太算。它是个成长和舒适生活的好地方，但为了有抱负的事业，年轻人常常得去大城市。这儿的机会比较有限。所以我会说它是个宜居的地方，但不是开启事业最好的地方。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":13,"en":"Yes, a bit. I know the main events — when the city was founded, why it's built along the river, and that it was an important trading spot long ago. Most of it I learned from my family and from visiting the city museum. So I have a general idea of its past, not every detail.","cn":"学过一点。我知道主要的event——城市何时建立、为什么沿河而建，以及很久以前它是重要的贸易点。大部分是我从家人和参观市博物馆时了解的。所以我对它的过去有个大致的了解，不是每个细节。"},{"b":"08","t":2,"i":14,"en":"Yes, in a casual way. My grandparents told me stories about local festivals and old customs — things like the food we eat on certain days and how people used to celebrate. It wasn't formal learning, but those stories taught me about the culture more than any textbook could.","cn":"学过，比较随意地。我爷爷奶奶跟我讲过本地节日和旧习俗的故事——比如某些日子吃什么、人们过去怎么庆祝。那不是正式的学习，但那些故事教给我的文化，比任何课本都多。"},{"b":"08","t":3,"i":0,"en":"Yes, I really like the area I live in. It's a quiet residential neighbourhood in the east of my city, with plenty of trees and a small park just five minutes' walk away. The best part is that it's convenient — there's a metro station and a big supermarket nearby, so I never have to travel far for daily necessities.","cn":"喜欢，我挺喜欢我住的这个区域。它是我所在城市东边的一个安静的居民区，绿化很多，步行五分钟就有一个小公园。最让我满意的是方便——附近有地铁站和大超市，日常买东西完全不用跑远。"},{"b":"08","t":3,"i":1,"en":"I usually go to the park near my home. I like to jog there in the early morning or just sit on a bench and read when the weather is nice. Sometimes I go to a small café around the corner with my friends — it's cosy and not too crowded, so we can chat for hours without being disturbed.","cn":"我经常去家附近的那个公园。早上我会去那儿慢跑，天气好的时候就坐在长椅上看看书。有时我也会和朋友去拐角的一家小咖啡馆，那儿环境温馨、人也不多，我们可以聊上好几个小时都不被打扰。"},{"b":"08","t":3,"i":2,"en":"Not really, no. I don't know anyone famous personally. My neighbourhood is quite ordinary — most people are just office workers, teachers or small shop owners. That said, I once saw a local TV presenter at the supermarket, but I didn't talk to her. It's not the kind of place where celebrities live.","cn":"其实并不认识。我本人不认识什么名人。我住的小区挺普通的，大多数居民就是普通上班族、老师或者小店主。不过我确实有一次在超市见过本地的一位电视主持人，但没上去说话。我们那儿不是名人扎堆的地方。"},{"b":"08","t":3,"i":3,"en":"Yes, quite a few changes actually. The biggest one is the new metro line that opened last year — it used to take me forty minutes to get downtown, now it's only fifteen. They've also renovated the old market and turned a piece of wasteland into a community garden, which makes the whole area look much nicer than before.","cn":"确实变化挺多的。最大的变化是去年新开通的地铁线——以前去市中心要四十分钟，现在只要十五分钟。他们还翻新了老菜市场，把一块荒地改成了社区花园，整个区域看起来比以前舒服多了。"},{"b":"08","t":3,"i":4,"en":"Yes, I know a few of them by sight. There's an elderly couple next door who always greet me when we meet in the corridor, and a young family with two kids who live upstairs. We're not close friends, but we help each other out — they once looked after my parcel when I was away.","cn":"认识几个，算是点头之交吧。隔壁住着一对老夫妻，在楼道里碰到总会跟我打招呼；楼上还有一户带着两个小孩的年轻家庭。我们算不上很熟，但会互相帮忙——我有一次出门，他们帮我收了快递。"},{"b":"08","t":3,"i":5,"en":"Yes, they're lovely. People here are quite warm and easy-going. When I moved in, my neighbours brought me some home-made snacks and told me where the best shops were. In the evenings, a lot of residents walk their dogs or play chess in the courtyard, and everyone usually says hello. It feels like a friendly little community.","cn":"是的，人都挺好的。这里的居民很热情也很随和。我刚搬来的时候，邻居给我送了自家做的小点心，还告诉我哪家店买什么最合适。傍晚很多人会在院子里遛狗或者下棋，大家见面都会打招呼。感觉就像个很有人情味的小社区。"},{"b":"08","t":3,"i":6,"en":"It's fairly quiet most of the time, which is exactly why I like it. There's not much traffic on my street, so at night it's really peaceful and I can sleep well. The only noisy moment is in the morning when the nearby primary school starts, but that only lasts about half an hour.","cn":"大部分时候挺安静的，这也是我喜欢这儿的原因。我这条街车流量不大，晚上特别安静，睡眠质量很好。唯一有点吵的是早上附近小学上学那会儿，不过也就持续半小时左右。"},{"b":"08","t":4,"i":0,"en":"I live in Nanjing, which is a historic city in the east of China, not far from Shanghai. It used to be the capital of several dynasties, so there are plenty of old sites like city walls and museums mixed with modern shopping centres. It's a nice balance between tradition and city life.","cn":"我住在南京，中国东部的一座历史名城，离上海不远。它曾经是好几个朝代的都城，所以既有城墙、博物馆这样的古迹，也有现代化的购物中心，传统和都市生活结合得挺好。"},{"b":"08","t":4,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I really like it. First, it's convenient — the public transport is excellent, so I can get almost anywhere by metro. Second, there's a lot to do: I can go to the museum, watch a concert or just wander around the old town. And the food here is fantastic, which honestly is a big reason I'd never want to move away.","cn":"很喜欢。第一是方便，公共交通特别好，坐地铁几乎哪儿都能去。第二是生活丰富，我可以去看展、听音乐会，或者随便在古城里逛逛。而且这里的美食真的很棒，老实说这是我不愿搬走的一大原因。"},{"b":"08","t":4,"i":2,"en":"I've lived here for about eight years now, since I came to university. So I've really seen the city change over time — I remember when the new metro lines hadn't been built yet and getting around was much slower. By now it feels like home rather than just a place I study in.","cn":"我在这儿住了大概八年了，从大学的时候算起。所以我是眼看着这座城市变化的——我记得那会儿新地铁线还没修好，出行慢得多。现在这儿对我来说已经像家一样，而不只是读书的地方。"},{"b":"08","t":4,"i":3,"en":"Yes, definitely. The city has grown very fast. A lot of new metro lines have opened, and whole new districts have been built with offices and apartment blocks. The old riverside area used to be quite run-down, but now it's been turned into a trendy place with cafés and walking paths. Sometimes I barely recognise parts of it.","cn":"变化非常大。城市发展得特别快，开通了很多新地铁线，还建起了好几个新的商务住宅区。以前的江边挺破旧的，现在改造成了有咖啡馆和步道的时髦区域。有时候我几乎认不出某些地方了。"},{"b":"08","t":4,"i":4,"en":"Yes, I'd say so. I've been here for eight years, I studied here, and my job is here too. My parents actually live in a smaller town nearby, so I still go back to visit them, but for now Nanjing is where I want to build my life. I can definitely see myself staying long-term.","cn":"算是吧。我在这儿待了八年，在这儿读书，工作也在这儿。我父母其实住在附近的一个小城市，我还会回去看他们，但眼下南京就是我想扎根的地方。我完全能想象自己长期留在这里。"},{"b":"08","t":4,"i":5,"en":"Yes, very much so. It's a university city, so there are lots of students in their twenties, but there are also plenty of families and retired people. In my neighbourhood, for instance, I see young couples pushing prams and elderly people doing tai chi in the morning. I think that mix makes the city feel lively but also stable.","cn":"是的，各种年龄的人都有。它是个大学城，所以有很多二十多岁的学生，但同时也有很多家庭和退休老人。比如在我住的小区，早上能看到年轻夫妻推着婴儿车，也能看到老人打太极。我觉得这种混搭让城市既有活力又很安定。"},{"b":"08","t":4,"i":6,"en":"Generally yes. People here are usually quite helpful, although we can be a bit reserved at first. Once you get to know them, though, they're very warm — for example, when I got lost in the old town, a shop owner walked me to the right bus stop instead of just giving me directions.","cn":"总的来说挺友好的。这里的人一般都很乐于帮忙，只是刚开始可能有点慢热。但熟悉之后就很热情——比如我在老城区迷路那次，一个店主直接把我带到了正确的公交站，而不是只指个方向。"},{"b":"08","t":4,"i":7,"en":"I'd say yes. There are quite a few parks with playgrounds, and the city has invested in things like children's libraries and sports centres. One thing I really notice is that public transport is free for elderly people, so you often see them out and about. That said, during rush hour the metro can be quite crowded for older people.","cn":"我觉得还算友好。有不少带游乐设施的公园，城市也投入建了儿童图书馆和体育中心。我特别注意到老年人坐公共交通是免费的，所以经常能看到他们出门。不过高峰期地铁对老人来说还是有点挤。"},{"b":"08","t":4,"i":8,"en":"Not very often, to be honest. In a big city like this, everyone is busy, and people tend to keep to themselves. I usually only see my neighbours in the lift or when we collect parcels. My parents' town is completely different — there, everyone knows everyone and chats on the street.","cn":"说实话不太常见。在这样的大城市里，大家都很忙，一般各过各的。我通常只在电梯里或者取快递的时候才会见到邻居。我父母住的小城市就完全不一样，那儿大家彼此都认识，在街上就能聊起来。"},{"b":"08","t":4,"i":9,"en":"It's quite mild, with four distinct seasons. Summers are hot and humid and can reach almost forty degrees, while winters are cold but rarely snowy. Spring and autumn are the nicest — cool and comfortable, and that's when I do most of my outdoor activities. The only downside is the rainy season in June, when it drizzles for days.","cn":"气候挺温和的，四季分明。夏天又热又潮，最高能接近四十度；冬天冷，但很少下雪。最舒服的是春秋两季，凉爽宜人，我的户外活动基本都安排在这时候。唯一的缺点是六月的梅雨季，会连着下好几天小雨。"},{"b":"08","t":4,"i":10,"en":"Yes, I'd happily recommend it. It's a good mix — it has the convenience and opportunities of a big city, but it's less crowded and less expensive than Shanghai. The history and the food alone make it worth a visit. The only thing I'd warn people about is the summer heat, so I'd suggest coming in spring or autumn.","cn":"会推荐，而且很乐意。它是个很好的折中选择——有大城市的便利和机会，但比上海没那么拥挤、花销也更低。光是历史和美食就值得来一趟。唯一要提醒的是夏天太热，所以我会建议春秋季来。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":0,"en":"I'm studying business administration at university. My main subjects are marketing, finance and organisational management, and I'm now in my final year. I also take some elective courses like data analysis, which I find surprisingly useful for my future career.","cn":"我在大学学的是工商管理。主要课程有市场营销、金融和组织管理，现在是大四。我还选了一些像数据分析这样的选修课，没想到对未来求职还挺有用的。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":1,"en":"Yes, I enjoy it most of the time. I like that it's practical — we work on real business cases and do group projects, so it doesn't feel like pure theory. Of course, the exam period can be stressful, especially when several deadlines fall in the same week, but overall I'm glad I chose it.","cn":"大部分时候挺喜欢的。我喜欢它很实用——我们会做真实的商业案例分析、小组项目，所以不完全是纸上谈兵。当然考试周压力会比较大，尤其是几个作业截止日期挤在同一周的时候，但总体我还是很庆幸选了这个专业。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":2,"en":"I chose it mainly out of interest, but also for practical reasons. I've always been curious about how companies work and why some succeed while others fail. At the same time, it's a broad subject — it opens up many career paths, like marketing, consulting or human resources, so I didn't have to lock myself into one narrow field at eighteen.","cn":"选它主要是出于兴趣，也有现实的考虑。我一直很好奇公司是怎么运作的，为什么有的成功有的失败。同时它也是个很宽泛的专业，能通向很多职业方向，比如市场营销、咨询或人力资源，所以十八岁的时候不用把自己限定在一个很窄的领域里。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":3,"en":"Yes, it's quite popular, though for a slightly practical reason — many students choose it because they think it leads to a stable office job. That also means there's a lot of competition, so a degree alone isn't enough; you really need internships and extra skills to stand out.","cn":"挺热门的，不过原因有点现实——很多学生选它是因为觉得将来能有个稳定的办公室工作。这也意味着竞争很激烈，光有文凭还不够，还得有实习经历和额外技能才能脱颖而出。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":4,"en":"Yes, I have a fairly clear plan. In the next two years I want to finish my degree with a good grade and hopefully get a job in marketing. After that, once I have some work experience, I'd like to take a master's degree, maybe abroad. So my short-term goal is to find a job, and my long-term goal is to keep studying part-time.","cn":"有比较清晰的规划。接下来两年我想以不错的成绩毕业，然后争取做市场营销方面的工作。之后等积累了一些工作经验，我想去读个硕士，可能出国。所以短期目标是找工作，长期目标是边工作边继续深造。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":5,"en":"I'd say the biggest benefit is having energy and few responsibilities. At this age I can stay up late, learn new things quickly and take risks — if I make a mistake now, it's much easier to recover from than later. But of course, the downside is that I don't have much money or experience yet.","cn":"我觉得最大的好处是有精力、负担少。这个年纪我可以熬夜、学新东西很快，也敢冒险——现在犯错，比以后犯错要容易补救得多。当然，不好的一面是还缺钱、缺经验。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":6,"en":"No, I don't think so. I know some people change their major because they realise they don't like it, but I actually enjoy mine. If anything, I'd rather deepen it — maybe specialise in marketing or add a minor in data analysis — than switch to something completely different.","cn":"不打算换。我知道有些人是因为发现不喜欢才转专业，但我其实挺喜欢自己的专业。如果要调整的话，我更想把它学深——比如专攻市场营销，或者辅修数据分析——而不是转到一个完全不相干的专业。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":7,"en":"Definitely in the mornings. I'm much more focused before lunch, especially between nine and eleven, when I can read and write for hours without getting distracted. In the afternoon I tend to feel sleepy, so I usually schedule lighter tasks like group discussions or reviewing notes. In the evening I can still work, but it takes more effort.","cn":"绝对是上午。我午前状态好得多，尤其是九点到十一点，能连着读写好几个小时不走神。下午我容易困，所以一般安排小组讨论或者复习笔记这类轻松点的事。晚上也能学，但要多费点劲。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":8,"en":"Probably around twenty hours a week outside class — so roughly three hours a day. That includes attending lectures, doing group projects and preparing for exams. During the exam period it can easily double, but I try to keep a balance so I don't burn out.","cn":"课外大概每周二十小时吧，差不多每天三小时，包括上课、做小组项目和备考。考试周翻倍都很正常，但我会尽量保持平衡，免得把自己熬垮。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":9,"en":"Yes and no. On one hand, I'm excited to earn my own money and stop relying on my parents, and I'm looking forward to applying what I've learnt in a real workplace. On the other hand, I'll miss the freedom of student life — the long holidays and the fact that you can make mistakes without serious consequences.","cn":"又期待又有点犹豫。一方面我很期待能自己赚钱、不再依赖父母，也想把学到的东西用到真实的工作里。另一方面，我会怀念学生时代的自由——长长的假期，还有犯错也不会有严重后果的那种轻松。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":10,"en":"Mainly my laptop and a few study apps. I use Notion to organise my notes and deadlines, and an app called Anki for memorising key terms through flashcards. When we do group projects, we usually collaborate on shared documents online. I'd say technology saves me a lot of time, though I still prefer paper for taking notes in class.","cn":"主要是笔记本电脑和几个学习App。我用Notion整理笔记和截止日期，用Anki这个软件通过卡片记忆专业术语。做小组项目时我们一般在共享文档上协作。我觉得科技帮我省了很多时间，不过上课记笔记我还是喜欢用纸。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":11,"en":"I'd like to see fewer exams and more practical projects. Right now we spend a lot of time memorising facts just to pass tests, and I forget most of it afterwards. I'd also like better career support — for example, more help finding internships and more advice from people actually working in the field.","cn":"我希望少一些考试、多一些实践项目。现在我们花很多时间背知识点只为通过考试，考完就忘得差不多了。我也希望学校有更好的就业支持，比如多帮忙找实习机会，多请真正在行业内工作的人来给建议。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":12,"en":"I work as a part-time marketing assistant at a small company. My main job is to help manage our social media accounts and write content for promotions. It's only about fifteen hours a week, so I can fit it around my studies, but it's given me a lot of hands-on experience.","cn":"我在一家小公司做兼职的市场助理。主要工作是帮忙管理社交媒体账号、写推广文案。每周大概十五小时，所以能兼顾学业，但也让我积累了不少实操经验。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":13,"en":"I chose it because it's directly related to my major, so I can apply what I learn in class to real work. Also, the company is small, which means I get to do a bit of everything instead of just one narrow task. And honestly, the flexible hours were a big plus for a student like me.","cn":"选这份工作是因为它和我的专业直接相关，能把课上学的东西用到实际工作中。另外公司比较小，意味着我什么都能接触到，而不只是做很单一的事。而且说实话，时间灵活这点对像我这样的学生来说太重要了。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":14,"en":"Yes, I do enjoy it. It's creative — I like coming up with ideas for posts and seeing how people respond. The team is friendly and my manager gives me useful feedback. The only thing I'm not so keen on is the repetitive part, like scheduling posts, but that's a small price to pay.","cn":"挺喜欢的。这份工作很有创造性——我喜欢想点子、发内容，然后看大家的反应。团队很友好，主管也会给我有用的反馈。唯一不太喜欢的是那些重复性工作，比如定时发帖，不过这点代价可以接受。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":15,"en":"Not many formal requirements, since it's an internship-level role. The main ones were basic writing skills, some familiarity with social media platforms, and being able to work in a team. They did ask about my major and whether I could commit to at least six months, but there was no strict exam or certificate needed.","cn":"因为算是实习级别的岗位，正式要求不多。主要就是基本的写作能力、对社交媒体平台有一定了解，以及能团队合作。他们问了我的专业、能不能至少做满六个月，但并没有严格的考试或证书要求。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":16,"en":"Yes, in the short term. In the next two years I want to keep this job while finishing my degree, and hopefully move from part-time to a full-time position after I graduate. In the longer term, maybe five years from now, I'd like to be in a more senior role, perhaps leading a small team or specialising in brand strategy.","cn":"有短期规划。接下来两年我想一边做这份工作一边完成学业，毕业后争取从兼职转成全职。再往长看，大概五年后，我希望做到更资深的岗位，比如带一个小团队，或者专攻品牌策略。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":17,"en":"At the moment, I'd say finishing my degree well is the most important thing. Everything else — the job, my hobbies — comes second, because my degree will shape what opportunities I get afterwards. I'm also trying to build good habits like exercising and sleeping properly, because I've learnt that without energy nothing else works.","cn":"目前来说，我觉得最重要的是把学位读好。其他事情——工作、爱好——都要往后排，因为学位会影响我之后能拿到什么机会。同时我也在努力养成好习惯，比如锻炼、规律睡眠，因为我发现没有精力的话什么都做不成。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":18,"en":"Not right now, but I wouldn't rule it out in the future. I'm still learning a lot here and the people are nice, so there's no strong reason to leave. If I ever felt I'd stopped growing, or if another company offered me a much better chance to develop, then yes, I'd probably consider moving.","cn":"现在不想，但以后也不排除。我在这儿还能学到很多东西，同事也很好，所以没什么理由离开。如果哪天我觉得自己不再成长了，或者有别的公司能给我更好的发展机会，那我大概会考虑换。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":19,"en":"A little, yes. I miss how simple life was — no deadlines from managers, long holidays, and the freedom to just explore subjects I found interesting. But at the same time, I enjoy the independence of earning my own money and being treated like an adult, so I wouldn't actually go back.","cn":"有一点吧。我会怀念那时候生活很简单——没有上司催的截止日期，有长长的假期，还能自由地去探索自己感兴趣的领域。但与此同时，我也享受自己赚钱、被当作成年人对待的那种独立感，所以真要回去我是不愿意的。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":20,"en":"Mostly the same tools as for studying — a laptop, plus some work apps. We use a project management tool to track tasks, and messaging apps to communicate with the team, especially when some colleagues work from home. I also use simple design software to make images for our social media posts.","cn":"基本和学习的工具差不多——一台笔记本，再加上一些办公App。我们用项目管理工具来跟踪任务，用聊天软件和团队沟通，尤其是有些同事居家办公的时候。我还会用一些简单的设计软件给社交媒体做图。"},{"b":"08","t":5,"i":21,"en":"Honestly, my mum helps me the most. She's the one I call when I'm stressed about exams or work, and she always listens without judging and then gives me calm, practical advice. My closest friend also helps a lot — she's in a similar situation, so we support each other by sharing notes and encouraging each other when things get tough.","cn":"说实话，帮我最多的是我妈妈。我因为考试或工作焦虑的时候都是打给她，她总是先耐心听我说，不评判，然后给我冷静又实在的建议。我最好的朋友也帮了我很多——她情况跟我差不多，所以我们会互相分享笔记、在艰难的时候互相打气。"}];